WEBVTT

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.480
It's morning?!

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.920
I'm heading up to the club room now.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.010
See you!

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:28.650
Bye-bye!

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.530
Sky high!

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.140
I won't do this.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.820
Afterschool Tea Time's music...

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.350
shouldn't sound anything like this!

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.360
But I want to go down this path.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.480
What was that?!

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.760
You'll ruin us, Yui! Ruin us!

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.440
Ruin us! Ruin us! Ruin us!

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:18.820
Ruin us! Ruin us! Ruin us!

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.740
Stop fighting! The two of you are friends!
Ruin us! Ruin us! Ruin us!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:20.760
Ruin us! Ruin us! Ruin us!

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.730
Ruin—

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.480
U-Um...

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.270
Did something happen?

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.380
The light music club might be breaking up.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.660
Breaking up?!

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.420
Why now of all times?

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.760
Everyone wants to take our music in a different direction.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.340
It's a matter of creative difference, Azu-nyan.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.140
Really? Creative difference?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:46.470
Is your "creative difference"
forgetting three chords to learn one?

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.500
At least I didn't fall down
and flash my panties on stage!

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.090
K-Keep that out of this!

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.100
Um...

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.570
I thought this was about creative difference.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.900
What do you think, Azusa-chan?

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.150
Oh, I...

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.570
I think that we should keep our cheerful, upbeat image.

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.490
You know, honestly...

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:07.780
This cutesy image of ours...

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:08.660
is getting old!

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.170
Don't even go there!

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.790
You joined with the words:
"The light music club plays light music, right?"

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:16.590
You came off as more than a few cards short of a deck!

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.170
Cards?

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:21.180
Yeah, and who was it who said I could just hang around while practically <i>begging</i> me to join?!

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.930
Hey, why don't we play old maid?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.680
Don't be foolish, Azusa!

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.180
The very fate of the club is on the line here!

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:28.810
Azu-nyan.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:29.560
Yes?!

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.180
Let's play later.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.380
So what?!

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.860
You joined anyway when you couldn't play guitar or even harmonica!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:38.580
Mhmot mffrue!

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.110
I can fway hahmonica!

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.400
Oh, really?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.450
Play something, then.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.130
I'm sorry. I can't play it!

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.050
You're all going nuts!

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:47.450
Mugi-chan?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.920
Mugi?

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.960
I-It's really all your fault for bringing sweets in the first place!

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.710
You sure care while stuffing yourself!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.800
I only do that because she brings yummy things!

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.550
I am <i>so</i> sorry for that.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:01.620
What?!

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.260
Say something, Mio-chan!

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:03.980
M-Me?!

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:04.760
It's Ritsu's fault!

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.760
Yeah!

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.480
Stupid Ricchan!

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.180
What did you just say?!

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.290
Isn't this what you were just play—

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.530
What are you doing?

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.200
Busted?

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.000
We're pretending to be Death Devil.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.960
That was so much fun!

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.250
Can we stop doing these little acts during rehearsal?

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.210
But you were so into it!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.970
You were just acting?

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:44.760
Yeah.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:49.430
We wanted to try the whole "creative differences" thing.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.970
It's a phase all bands go through.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.640
Right?
I figured it was something like that.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.730
I figured it was something like that.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.060
So now that Azusa-chan's here...

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:58.920
I'll be ready in a second.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.640
How about some tea?

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.180
Huh?

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:04.400
What?

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.720
Let's go over our performance just now.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:56.560
I thought she'd be a little more surprised.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.020
So you're not going over rehearsal?

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.150
I already fed Ton-chan.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:04.980
Thank you.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.570
I don't think we were very convincing.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.920
That "You're all going nuts" of yours felt especially out of place.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.490
Don't worry about it.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.580
That's not something you say to yourself.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:21.460
I had no idea what I was signing up
for when I joined this club.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.580
Look who's getting sassy!

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.960
That tea you're drinking!

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:28.920
It's a one-of-a-kind light music club special!

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.880
It's the Kotobuki family's treasured tea!

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:33.760
I'm sorry.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:34.680
It's delicious.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:35.820
Nice, Mugi!

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:36.930
You brought Baumkuchen?

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.390
Let's peel it apart layer by layer.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:40.400
Don't say that!

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.350
It sounds painful.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.440
Open it already, Mugi!

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.190
It's too tight...

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.660
<i>For three years now,</i>

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.720
<i>we've been eating sweets,</i>

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.800
<i>drinking tea,</i>

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:51.610
<i>and practicing together in this room.</i>

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.620
Nothing left but graduation now, huh?

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.750
While that is true, should you really be slacking off now?

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.460
Why not? We already got accepted into college!

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.880
Right, Ricchan?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.630
Miracles really do exist.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:09.090
Mio-senpai and Mugi-senpai aside.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:09.410
Hey—

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.120
Just how little faith does she have in us?
Mugi-senpai, I have scissors if you need them.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.290
Mugi-senpai, I have scissors if you need them.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.660
Yui-senpai...

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.070
Cute, isn't it?

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.810
It finally opened!

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.150
So with that out of the way...

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.570
I'm glad we all got into the same college.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.650
Come on, cheers!

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.930
You too, Azu-nyan.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.990
O-Okay...

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:38.990
Cheers!

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:41.160
Cheers!

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:43.710
Sawa-chan?!

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.560
That's one less thing for me to worry about.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.780
I'm glad that you all passed your exams.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.970
It must be stressful being the homeroom teacher of a graduating class.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.880
Still, time sure flies.

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.930
I can hardly believe you're all graduating.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:05.100
How much tea do you think we've drank over the last three years?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.380
At least a thousand cups.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.700
A grand!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.860
We truly are Afterschool Tea Time.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.930
We sure lived up to our band name.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.410
Well, all that's left now is sending you off!

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.870
So long as no one's repeating.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:20.910
Repeating?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:21.930
Yeah.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.020
We're holding a meeting next week.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:32.920
We'll be reviewing attendance records and exam scores.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.510
There's such an important meeting?

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.600
S-Sawa-chan!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.720
We were just imitating Death Devil!

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.320
Death Devil rules!

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:47.020
The best band formed by the best teacher!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.540
S-So...

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.190
So?

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:54.110
A-As an ex-member of the light music club...

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.490
...gore easy on us!

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.860
That sounded a little weird.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.310
It's a little too late for that now.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:09:59.480
Please!
It's a little too late for that now.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.870
Grandmaster Yamanaka Sawako!

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.580
What's the matter?

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.050
Is what Sawa-chan said on your mind?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.470
It's not that.

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.420
So what, then?

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.530
This has her name written all over it.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:37.780
I feel like we're about to graduate
without proving ourselves as seniors.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.450
What?!

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.030
That's not true!

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:42.030
We're...

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.320
Taller!

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:44.410
Older!

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.520
Lively!

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.330
Can't you think of anything else?

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:48.320
I...

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:52.210
want to do one last thing for her before we graduate.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:57.700
I like the sound of that!

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:58.560
Let's do it!

00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:59.470
Nice one, Yui!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.720
What should we do?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.060
How about some kind of present?

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.390
Something that feels very Azu-nyan.

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:10.900
Found them.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.230
This is so exciting!

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.890
Keep this a secret, okay?

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.170
There you are!

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:17.900
Azu-nyan!

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.990
You left a trail of trash behind you.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:25.280
I thought we might get lost on
the way back to the club room...

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.580
I picked it all up.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.660
We'll never find our way back now!

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.280
Of course you will.

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:32.420
Come on, let's go.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.390
Okay!

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.300
Something that'd make Azusa-chan happy?

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.430
Yeah.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.350
It can be a thing, words, or whatever.

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:53.020
Hmm, let's see...

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.460
Hasn't she said anything to you?

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.190
You're in the same class.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:12:00.610
You know, like how cool we are or something.

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:02.280
Well...

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.780
C'mon, tell me!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:10.370
She's said that she wants you all to take practice a bit more seriously.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:15.080
And that it'd be nice if the club room were kept just a bit cleaner.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.980
Oh, and that you shouldn't hug her so much.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.210
Onee-chan!

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:23.720
Nothing new there.

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:31.270
It's a wonder she's stuck with us so long.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.020
But still...

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:37.230
All she ever talks about is the light music club!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.270
Really?

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:39.770
Really.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:47.990
Besides, she only joined the light music club because she heard you guys playing.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:50.980
I guess she did say that.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:53.610
I know!

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:57.380
Maybe you should stay back
a year and graduate with her.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:01.510
Maybe...

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:05.010
I was just kidding, Onee-chan!

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:22.240
Azu-nyan...

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:28.230
What do you want?!

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.320
Yui-chan!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:48.130
Ah, Mugi-chan! Morning!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:51.100
I see Gitah-chan left you some love marks.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.970
We slept together!

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.420
It's cold!

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.270
Let me hold your hand, Mugi-chan.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.520
Sure.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:00.650
Ritsu, Ritsu!

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:01.520
Yeah?

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.230
I wrote some new lyrics before I went to bed last night!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.780
Oh, a new song?

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.400
"Ice Cream Love"?

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.160
Let's get Mugi to put music to it!

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:12.160
Ricchan! Mio-chan!

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:14.410
Happy morning!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:15.580
G'morning!

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.870
Mugi-chan's hand was so warm that I started sweating!

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:22.460
Akiyama-san's hand was so cold that I almost froze to death!

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:23.550
What's that supposed to mean?

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.920
Think of anything for Azu-nyan yet?

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:27.760
Did you?

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.170
I fell asleep while trying to think of something.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:31.100
Me too!

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:32.680
I fell asleep with my socks still on.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.310
I strip bare when I sleep.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.350
You what?!

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.340
Mio-chan's all grown up!

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:39.310
I was talking about my socks!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.500
The sooner we book,
the better, don't you think?

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:40.590
Morning! Everyone's here so early.
The sooner we book,
the better, don't you think?

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:41.840
Okay.
Morning! Everyone's here so early.
The sooner we book,
the better, don't you think?

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:42.730
Morning! Everyone's here so early.
The sooner we book,
the better, don't you think?

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:42.800
School's the only place we can all see each other.
The sooner we book,
the better, don't you think?

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.940
School's the only place we can all see each other.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.070
That's a pretty good idea.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.490
Morning, Nodoka-chan!

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.020
Oh, good morning.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.520
How's tomorrow sound?

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:55.740
We can go swimsuit shopping afterward.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:58.080
I've never been to Hawaii before!

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:00.580
Did you hear Hawaii too, Mugi-chan?

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:01.670
Yeah.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.550
Hey, are you all going to Hawaii?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:06.960
Yeah, for our graduation trip.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.780
Is the light music club going anywhere?

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.510
Ricchan!

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:13.640
Whatcha want?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.600
So about the guidebooks...

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.720
We'll need to get one for everyone on the team.
The volleyball team is going on a graduation trip.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:18.770
Really?

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:20.860
We should go somewhere too!

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:22.440
When are you leaving?

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:24.820
A week before the ceremony.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.320
Travel's cheaper around then.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.150
How about it, Ricchan?

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:30.240
That's right before spring break.

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.240
We should totally go somewhere!

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.180
Nope, no way!

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.240
We'll do our thing, and they'll do theirs!

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:44.250
Right now, we should focus on
thinking of something for Azusa.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.420
Can I have everyone's attention?

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:50.170
I was thinking that we should all do something for Sawako-sensei on the day of the ceremony.

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:51.760
Any ideas what?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.720
Oh, and please keep this a secret from her.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:54.840
What do you think?

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.560
Something that'll make her cry?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.470
We could sing the school song!

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:02.860
What does Sawako-sensei like?

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:04.310
Good question.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:05.560
So...

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:08.610
I think we should go on a graduation trip!

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:10.780
Here we go.

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:14.410
I thought about it some more
and realized we all have our passports.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:18.370
You <i>just</i> said we should focus on thinking of something for Azusa.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.910
We can do that too!

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.540
Be serious for once!

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:26.380
You're always leaving things to the last minute.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.960
A little waiting never hurt anyone, Ms. Stickler!

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.010
I interviewed Ui about it.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.340
Care to share the details with us?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.600
Okay, Ui said...

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:37.800
Wait a second.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:38.600
What's that?

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.760
It's from the Scrolls of Frolicking Animals!

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:42.600
I saw it in our textbook the other—

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.650
So back to what Ui-chan said.

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:49.900
Ui said that maybe we should stay back a year

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:53.320
and graduate with her.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.110
So her present would be us repeating a year?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:58.700
Yup, repeating a year!

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:03.580
What's going on?

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:04.710
Nothing really.

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:06.710
You're obviously hiding something.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:07.710
Oh, really now?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.630
And did she just mention repeating a year?

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:13.340
Life gives us all our own challenges.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.220
Where did you hear that, Azusa-chan?

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.600
"Where"? Yui-senpai just said it.

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:18.860
You misheard it.

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:20.460
Your ears are playing tricks on you.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.780
It was all in your head.

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.020
What are you doing?

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:26.850
We're trying to decide where to go on our graduation trip.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:30.360
So we were talking about meeting in Peer, a city in Belgium.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:30.900
What?!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.570
Such an ominous misunderstanding!

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:33.610
We're not going there!

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:36.810
Oh, so you're going on a graduation trip?

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.580
Dubai!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.870
What happened to Hawaii?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:48.830
Dubai!

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:50.130
Europe!

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:51.960
A hot spring!

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.340
I want to play ping-pong.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.350
What about you, Mio-chan?

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:56.380
Me?

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.420
London, I guess.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:03.220
It's the hometown of many musicians,

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:04.810
and it has a rich history of music too.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.440
You're all over the world, huh?

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:07.980
What about you, Azu-nyan?

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:11.820
I'm not graduating yet, so it doesn't matter.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:19.780
When did we decide to go on a trip anyway?

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:22.280
It's where the river took us.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.290
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.910
Don't you want to go, Mio-chan?

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:28.920
I <i>do</i> want to, but...

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:29.760
How about this?

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.590
All in favor of not going on a trip, speak up now!

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.550
Crickets.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.920
Ton-chan.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:36.880
It's unanimous!

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.630
What an unbelievable way to decide.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.880
Let's decide where to go with a lottery!

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:45.520
I'm actually pretty good at lotteries.

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.180
What does that even mean?

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.580
One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:49.690
It's done!
One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.610
Now, if you will, President Tainaka Ritsu-san!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.420
Little ol' me?

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:56.680
Let's start... right here!

00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:57.280
Let's start... right here!

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:58.260
All right!

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:01.100
Now, where shall we end up?

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:16.950
The results are in!

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:18.800
We're going to Europe!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:22.940
Congratulations, Yui-chan!

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:26.010
But where in Europe are we going?

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.350
Ask Yui.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:28.020
Yui-senpai.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:29.060
Yeah?

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:31.810
Mind if I see that paper?

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:34.150
Wh-Why?

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.770
No reason really.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.570
Um...

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:41.530
She fled!

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.250
She fell!

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:49.240
Yui!

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:50.410
Yui-chan?

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:51.990
Yui?

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:52.940
Yui...

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.210
Yui!

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.470
Ricchan...

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:01.680
Yui!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:06.680
Look... I finally did it...

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:08.200
You did it!

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:09.420
You did well, Yui!

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:10.100
Ricchan...

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.040
I knew it.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:15.650
It was fixed.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:16.360
What?!

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:17.820
Oh, no!

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:21.030
You're way too predictable.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.740
You little cheat.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:25.210
You're incredible, Yui-chan!

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:27.450
That's not praise.

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:30.410
I guess I made a <i>tiny</i> mistake.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.330
Keep that on for a while.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.360
Yui.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.510
Okay, it's about time we made up our minds.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:47.410
We all want to go to difference places.

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:49.310
How about a vote?

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.140
I can see the results now.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:53.660
Why don't we leave it to Ton-chan?

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:56.980
Give it a rest.

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:01.110
Which teacup will Ton-chan choose?

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:01.610
Right.

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.990
It's like his own little amusement park!

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:06.160
By the way...

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:06.910
Yeah?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:10.540
Is it just me, or is the Europe cup kinda small?

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.790
Cheaters always get what's coming to them.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.120
I see...

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:22.130
<i>I never thought Ton-chan would have
such a big responsibility placed on him.</i>

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:26.800
Ton-chan's swimming high today.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.390
He doesn't care about the teacups.

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.850
Nice weather today.

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.980
They've lost interest already!

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:44.520
T-Ton-chan's...

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:46.380
swimming in front of Europe!

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:49.200
Oh, but he's touching London!

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:53.330
So we're going to London?

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:53.830
Yeah.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:59.170
London's in Europe. You should be happy.

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:00.160
Really?

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:03.250
Just how big is Europe?

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:06.840
I feel sorry for the college you're attending.

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:08.500
Mio!

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:10.350
We're going to London!

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:12.520
Isn't that great, Mio-chan?

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:15.520
Yes!

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:16.890
Mio-chan?
Mio?!

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:17.960
I can't believe it.

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:18.760
London!

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:20.650
I can't believe it!

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:22.820
We get it already. Relax.

00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:26.190
L-L-Lo... London!

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:30.870
You really wanted to go there, huh, Mio-chan?

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:34.000
London's the perfect place to have afternoon tea.

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:36.660
We can drink tea in London?

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:39.040
It's the tea capital of the world.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:42.400
Wow, it's like it was made for us!

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:46.420
We'll probably need two rooms for the five of us.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:47.550
Split three and two?

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:48.470
Yeah.

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:49.050
What?

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:51.140
You're coming with us, right?

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:52.380
No, I couldn't!

00:22:52.380 --> 00:22:54.770
It's your graduation trip, not mine!

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.430
Did you lose your passport?

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:57.920
No, I have it.

00:22:57.920 --> 00:22:59.640
But I still have school.

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:02.520
There's a break after finals, right?

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:05.080
I think we have five days off.

00:23:05.080 --> 00:23:07.090
There you go!

00:23:07.090 --> 00:23:08.070
But...

00:23:08.540 --> 00:23:10.490
I want to go with you!

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:13.990
The light music club isn't complete without you!

00:23:16.930 --> 00:23:19.710
Do you not want to go, Azusa?

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:21.420
I do want to!

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:25.210
But are you sure I won't just be a fifth wheel?

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:27.050
Why would you be?

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:31.820
I guess I'll go, then.

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:33.080
All right!

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:34.440
Let's do this!

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:38.060
Let me ask my parents before you get too excited.

00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:43.120
Hey, Mom.

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:44.810
It's Azusa.

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:47.170
Yeah, so...

00:23:51.640 --> 00:23:53.340
Thanks, Mom!

00:24:00.220 --> 00:24:02.370
My mom said I could go.

00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:04.500
Yeah, London.

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.670
It's for our graduation trip.

00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:08.840
Oh, Mama?

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:11.420
Please, Mom! I'll never ask for anything ever again!

00:24:11.420 --> 00:24:12.460
Yeah. Ritsu will be there, so I'll be fine.

00:24:12.460 --> 00:24:13.970
Really?
Yeah. Ritsu will be there, so I'll be fine.

00:24:14.590 --> 00:24:15.520
Thanks!

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:16.730
See you tonight.

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:24.350
I have to keep it together.

00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:31.040
You actually meant the city of London?

00:24:31.840 --> 00:24:33.220
Obviously!

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:37.370
What other London is there, Nodoka-chan?

00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:43.250
Your random text made me think it was some kind of shop.

00:24:43.250 --> 00:24:46.920
We're going to a travel agency together tomorrow.

00:24:46.920 --> 00:24:52.800
You're the last people I'd imagine longing England.

00:24:52.800 --> 00:24:54.620
Upsy-daisy!

00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:57.760
That's a new look.

00:24:57.760 --> 00:25:00.940
It was Mio-chan who wanted to go,

00:25:00.940 --> 00:25:03.140
but Ton-chan made the decision.

00:25:03.140 --> 00:25:04.890
Your soft-shelled turtle did?

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:06.840
<i>Pig-nosed</i> turtle!

00:25:06.840 --> 00:25:10.570
And we're going to London, not England!

00:25:12.400 --> 00:25:16.070
Yui, I hate to break it to you, but...

00:25:16.450 --> 00:25:18.490
London's in England.

00:25:20.580 --> 00:25:21.900
This is way too sudden!

00:25:21.900 --> 00:25:24.920
I didn't think I'd be going too.

00:25:24.920 --> 00:25:27.070
You're sure buying a lot.

00:25:27.960 --> 00:25:31.340
If I don't do the research, no one will.

00:25:35.190 --> 00:25:37.390
Take care of my sister, okay?

00:25:37.390 --> 00:25:38.320
Hey, Ui.

00:25:39.080 --> 00:25:41.750
About that sister of yours...

00:25:42.220 --> 00:25:46.140
I feel like she's hiding something from me.

00:25:46.800 --> 00:25:48.940
Do you know anything?

00:25:49.520 --> 00:25:53.630
I don't think she could hide
something even if she wanted to.

00:25:54.290 --> 00:25:55.900
I hear you there.

00:25:56.670 --> 00:25:57.780
Welcome!

00:25:58.050 --> 00:26:00.280
Are you looking to travel with us?

00:26:00.280 --> 00:26:01.580
Uh, yes!

00:26:01.580 --> 00:26:04.330
Um... Five days in London.

00:26:04.940 --> 00:26:07.240
Five days, three nights in London, correct?

00:26:07.240 --> 00:26:08.020
Three?

00:26:08.480 --> 00:26:09.640
How does that work?

00:26:09.640 --> 00:26:11.710
One night each way.

00:26:11.710 --> 00:26:13.140
Oh, yeah!

00:26:13.140 --> 00:26:13.880
I knew that!

00:26:13.880 --> 00:26:14.380
Of course!

00:26:14.380 --> 00:26:16.420
Is visiting only the city itself fine?

00:26:16.860 --> 00:26:17.920
Sound good?

00:26:17.920 --> 00:26:19.200
Sure, why not?

00:26:19.200 --> 00:26:20.400
It's more than fine!

00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:22.760
There's a lot to see in the city alone.

00:26:22.760 --> 00:26:24.020
I wanna ride that thing!

00:26:24.020 --> 00:26:25.560
Let's visit a tea house.

00:26:25.560 --> 00:26:27.740
Wow, that looks yummy!

00:26:27.740 --> 00:26:28.170
It does!

00:26:28.170 --> 00:26:29.830
That's so cool!

00:26:29.830 --> 00:26:33.580
I want to visit the homes of
Jimi Hendrix and Jimmy Page!

00:26:33.580 --> 00:26:34.360
Sounds fun!

00:26:34.360 --> 00:26:35.840
And David Bowie's too!

00:26:35.840 --> 00:26:37.230
Look, an instrument shop!

00:26:37.230 --> 00:26:38.120
Abbey Road!

00:26:38.120 --> 00:26:39.200
Excuse me.

00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:43.820
If you'd like to go sightseeing, I recommend booking without a travel itinerary.

00:26:44.380 --> 00:26:46.000
No, that'd be a bit...

00:26:46.430 --> 00:26:48.410
We'll do that, then!

00:27:04.430 --> 00:27:06.350
Morning!

00:27:06.370 --> 00:27:08.450
Oh, little girl from the light music club.

00:27:08.450 --> 00:27:10.230
It's cold, huh?

00:27:10.720 --> 00:27:13.360
So the occult club is still doing its thing?

00:27:13.360 --> 00:27:14.420
Yes.

00:27:14.420 --> 00:27:19.030
We're on our way to the roof to attempt contact with alien lifeforms.

00:27:19.030 --> 00:27:20.060
Oh, right!

00:27:20.060 --> 00:27:22.810
The light music club is going to England!

00:27:22.810 --> 00:27:23.950
That's nice.

00:27:23.950 --> 00:27:26.130
We're going for our graduation trip!

00:27:26.130 --> 00:27:28.110
Want me to get you anything?

00:27:30.180 --> 00:27:31.530
Nessie's...

00:27:31.530 --> 00:27:32.690
What?

00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:37.700
Nessie...

00:27:38.930 --> 00:27:41.760
Take a picture of Nessie for us.

00:27:41.760 --> 00:27:43.420
You got it!

00:27:43.420 --> 00:27:45.490
I'll get you that picture!

00:27:47.180 --> 00:27:49.090
Little girl...

00:27:49.450 --> 00:27:53.440
So do you think we can fit that in somewhere?

00:27:54.130 --> 00:27:55.880
You want to go see Nessie?

00:27:57.700 --> 00:28:00.150
Loch Ness is some ways off from London.

00:28:00.520 --> 00:28:03.620
And I hear that Nessie doesn't really exist.

00:28:03.620 --> 00:28:06.040
Wait, were they playing with me?

00:28:06.520 --> 00:28:10.000
Their jokes are way too hard to understand!

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:11.960
Now, now, Hirasawa-san.

00:28:11.960 --> 00:28:12.580
Ooh...

00:28:12.580 --> 00:28:15.490
Any other requests?

00:28:15.490 --> 00:28:16.950
Nope!

00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:22.470
I'll make an itinerary with all of this in mind, then.

00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:24.400
Will you be fine by yourself?

00:28:24.400 --> 00:28:25.260
Yes.

00:28:25.260 --> 00:28:27.320
I actually enjoy this kind of thing.

00:28:27.320 --> 00:28:28.490
All right, thanks.

00:28:28.490 --> 00:28:30.520
Do you want more tea, Azusa-chan?

00:28:30.520 --> 00:28:31.840
No, thank you.

00:28:31.840 --> 00:28:33.920
I'm already stuffed.

00:28:33.920 --> 00:28:38.360
We're going to have barely any snack time with Azu-nyan behind the schedule.

00:28:38.790 --> 00:28:43.070
What ever happened to traveling without an itinerary?

00:28:43.070 --> 00:28:44.360
Heading home, Azusa?

00:28:44.360 --> 00:28:45.180
Yes.

00:28:45.180 --> 00:28:47.780
Are you staying awhile longer?

00:28:47.780 --> 00:28:49.790
I'm going home!

00:28:52.270 --> 00:28:55.500
Not before practicing afternoon tea, though!

00:28:56.210 --> 00:28:57.090
We're...

00:28:57.090 --> 00:28:58.040
Yes?!

00:28:58.040 --> 00:29:01.050
We're going to stay for another cup of tea, Azusa-chan!

00:29:01.050 --> 00:29:02.220
This is for you.

00:29:02.760 --> 00:29:04.380
I hope you like it.

00:29:04.380 --> 00:29:05.970
We'll wash your cup too.

00:29:06.340 --> 00:29:07.600
Thanks.

00:29:07.600 --> 00:29:08.930
I'll let you do that.

00:29:08.930 --> 00:29:10.430
Be safe, Azusa!

00:29:10.430 --> 00:29:12.180
Don't go easy on the snack times!

00:29:12.180 --> 00:29:13.690
I'll take my leave, then.

00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:15.520
See you tomorrow!

00:29:16.690 --> 00:29:17.890
Now then...

00:29:18.850 --> 00:29:21.190
...let the show begin!

00:29:21.190 --> 00:29:22.110
What show?

00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:24.030
You're still here?!

00:29:24.030 --> 00:29:25.530
Hey, come on!

00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:27.370
Oh, you, Sawa-chan!

00:29:27.370 --> 00:29:29.030
I hope you like it!

00:29:29.030 --> 00:29:30.080
Oh, right!

00:29:30.080 --> 00:29:32.200
Didn't you have a date tonight?

00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:33.830
I have no such plans!

00:29:33.830 --> 00:29:35.580
You little joker!

00:29:37.970 --> 00:29:38.790
All righty.

00:29:39.290 --> 00:29:42.800
So what kind of present...

00:29:43.400 --> 00:29:44.720
should we get Azu-nyan?

00:29:44.720 --> 00:29:47.090
She's done so much for us over the years.

00:29:47.660 --> 00:29:53.390
So, how can we repay her for that in our own special way?

00:29:53.390 --> 00:29:54.220
How about a play?

00:29:54.220 --> 00:29:54.620
No more plays!

00:29:54.620 --> 00:29:55.520
Anything that could give us a hint?
No more plays!

00:29:55.520 --> 00:29:56.960
Anything that could give us a hint?

00:29:58.110 --> 00:30:00.190
Azu-nyan left Muttan behind!

00:30:00.650 --> 00:30:02.390
Poor Muttan!

00:30:02.390 --> 00:30:04.040
It's Mustang.

00:30:04.540 --> 00:30:07.120
Yours is Elizabeth, right?

00:30:10.100 --> 00:30:12.650
How about we ask Muttan?

00:30:13.340 --> 00:30:14.410
Muttan!

00:30:15.790 --> 00:30:19.380
Do you know what kind of present Azu-nyan would like?

00:30:19.840 --> 00:30:21.040
As if, right?

00:30:22.460 --> 00:30:23.130
Muttan!

00:30:24.410 --> 00:30:25.750
No! W-Wait!

00:30:28.720 --> 00:30:29.840
Muttan...

00:30:29.840 --> 00:30:30.720
Go on!

00:30:31.540 --> 00:30:33.020
He said a song.

00:30:33.020 --> 00:30:33.760
Oh no!

00:30:33.760 --> 00:30:35.810
She hit her head too hard!

00:30:35.810 --> 00:30:36.600
A songbook?

00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:37.980
No!

00:30:37.980 --> 00:30:38.690
A song...

00:30:38.690 --> 00:30:39.400
...writer?

00:30:39.400 --> 00:30:40.920
No!

00:30:40.920 --> 00:30:41.920
A song...

00:30:41.920 --> 00:30:42.480
...bird!

00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:46.700
No, singing! Music!

00:30:47.220 --> 00:30:50.990
Why did it take me so long to think of this?

00:30:50.990 --> 00:30:54.120
Are you saying we should write a song for Azusa?

00:30:54.600 --> 00:30:55.450
Exactly!

00:30:55.450 --> 00:30:57.370
Ui even told me...

00:30:57.370 --> 00:31:02.210
Azu-nyan loves the light music club and its music!

00:31:04.330 --> 00:31:06.630
A song for Azusa-chan?

00:31:08.050 --> 00:31:09.800
I can totally get behind that!

00:31:09.800 --> 00:31:10.620
Right?!

00:31:10.620 --> 00:31:12.580
A song left behind by her seniors?

00:31:12.580 --> 00:31:14.140
It sounds so cool!

00:31:14.140 --> 00:31:15.680
Yeah, it does!

00:31:16.350 --> 00:31:17.500
Hey, Yui.

00:31:17.500 --> 00:31:18.770
What kind of song should it be?

00:31:19.100 --> 00:31:22.980
It's a song from her seniors, so it needs to be like...

00:31:22.980 --> 00:31:24.300
Bam!

00:31:24.300 --> 00:31:25.690
And bang!

00:31:25.690 --> 00:31:27.180
And kaboom!

00:31:27.180 --> 00:31:28.400
You know?

00:31:28.400 --> 00:31:29.200
Not at all.

00:31:29.690 --> 00:31:34.840
Basically, it needs to be bigger than anything we've ever done before!

00:31:37.850 --> 00:31:40.000
And how do we do that?

00:31:45.700 --> 00:31:47.170
I can't believe I forgot him!

00:31:47.620 --> 00:31:49.740
Good morning!

00:31:50.300 --> 00:31:51.760
Just kidding.

00:31:53.460 --> 00:31:54.920
Azu-nyan?! When did you get there?!

00:31:54.920 --> 00:31:57.140
Um... I just got here...

00:31:57.140 --> 00:31:58.480
Really?!

00:31:58.480 --> 00:31:59.640
Yes!

00:32:03.310 --> 00:32:04.310
That was close.

00:32:04.310 --> 00:32:06.160
Oh, I get it!

00:32:06.160 --> 00:32:08.690
You came back for Muttan!

00:32:09.100 --> 00:32:11.780
You can't forget something so important!

00:32:11.780 --> 00:32:12.610
R-Right...

00:32:13.990 --> 00:32:15.640
Goodbye.

00:32:15.640 --> 00:32:17.540
Bye-bye!

00:32:25.730 --> 00:32:27.180
Nothing unusual.

00:32:27.840 --> 00:32:28.920
Azu-nyan?

00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:30.960
Silly me! What am I doing?

00:32:30.960 --> 00:32:33.180
Sorry! It's nothing!

00:32:33.180 --> 00:32:34.980
Goodbye!

00:32:40.600 --> 00:32:45.680
I've never seen them look so serious before.

00:32:51.210 --> 00:32:52.500
Something's going on.

00:33:00.650 --> 00:33:01.290
It's Mugi.

00:33:08.630 --> 00:33:10.510
She's sure having fun with this.

00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:13.180
I'm pretty nervous.

00:33:21.370 --> 00:33:24.980
We'll make this song a worldwide sensation!

00:33:30.460 --> 00:33:33.200
Hold this down for me, Onee-chan.

00:33:33.200 --> 00:33:33.650
Okay.

00:33:34.990 --> 00:33:36.710
It won't fit!

00:33:36.710 --> 00:33:38.940
We're packing lots of Japanese food.

00:33:38.940 --> 00:33:40.490
You'll miss it after awhile.

00:33:42.120 --> 00:33:44.120
You're taking your school uniform?

00:33:44.120 --> 00:33:45.790
We're all bringing them.

00:33:45.790 --> 00:33:46.780
I see.

00:33:46.780 --> 00:33:47.500
Yui.

00:33:47.500 --> 00:33:50.800
You should take this English phrasebook with you.

00:33:50.800 --> 00:33:51.960
Thanks!

00:33:51.960 --> 00:33:54.220
And here's an outlet converter and transformer.

00:33:54.220 --> 00:33:54.840
Thanks!

00:33:54.840 --> 00:33:56.340
Even more to squeeze in...

00:33:56.720 --> 00:33:58.100
Go to bed early tonight.

00:33:58.100 --> 00:33:59.140
You too, Ui.

00:33:59.140 --> 00:34:00.580
Okay!

00:34:03.220 --> 00:34:06.130
This time tomorrow, I'll be in London.

00:34:07.070 --> 00:34:08.650
You're so lucky!

00:34:08.650 --> 00:34:11.380
I'd feel better if you came along too.

00:34:13.410 --> 00:34:14.740
I don't think you'd fit.

00:34:14.740 --> 00:34:15.400
What?!

00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:16.530
Just kidding.

00:34:16.530 --> 00:34:18.320
Onee-chan!

00:34:18.320 --> 00:34:20.240
See you next week!

00:34:21.340 --> 00:34:24.000
Have a safe trip, Onee-chan!

00:34:24.490 --> 00:34:25.910
I'm going to go get a drink.

00:34:25.910 --> 00:34:26.660
All right.

00:34:26.660 --> 00:34:28.040
Watch my luggage for me.

00:34:28.040 --> 00:34:29.460
You got it!

00:34:34.110 --> 00:34:35.800
Ricchan, Ricchan!

00:34:35.800 --> 00:34:37.470
Mornin'!

00:34:37.470 --> 00:34:39.300
Hey!

00:34:39.300 --> 00:34:40.490
You brought Gitah?

00:34:40.490 --> 00:34:43.830
I was thinking that we should take pictures together.

00:34:43.830 --> 00:34:45.400
First Mio, now you.

00:34:45.400 --> 00:34:46.210
What's that mean?

00:34:46.210 --> 00:34:47.140
Nothing really.

00:34:48.160 --> 00:34:49.850
Now Azusa too.

00:34:52.820 --> 00:34:54.130
Good morning!

00:34:54.130 --> 00:34:55.570
Morning!

00:34:56.600 --> 00:34:58.570
So you brought Mustang along.

00:34:58.570 --> 00:34:59.580
Yeah.

00:34:59.580 --> 00:35:03.490
I almost didn't, but I was sure Yui-senpai would bring Gitah.

00:35:04.580 --> 00:35:05.610
Called it.

00:35:05.610 --> 00:35:07.500
So Yui and Azusa are here now.

00:35:08.900 --> 00:35:10.090
I knew it.

00:35:10.680 --> 00:35:14.550
If we run into any musicians,
we should ask if they'll sign them.

00:35:14.550 --> 00:35:16.090
Yeah, sure.

00:35:16.090 --> 00:35:18.970
Let's go meet Mugi at her station now.

00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:22.610
Up we go!

00:35:23.340 --> 00:35:25.600
So Ricchan brought her drumsticks too!

00:35:26.060 --> 00:35:28.100
Did you forget anything?

00:35:28.470 --> 00:35:30.900
I forgot my passport!

00:35:30.900 --> 00:35:33.040
Looks like we're leaving you behind.

00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:33.400
Wai—

00:35:33.400 --> 00:35:35.900
It's hanging from your neck.

00:35:37.530 --> 00:35:39.320
I've always wanted to try that.

00:35:54.470 --> 00:35:56.250
Morning, Mugi-chan!

00:35:56.250 --> 00:35:57.960
Morning!

00:35:58.980 --> 00:36:02.740
Nobody told me we were bringing them!

00:36:07.100 --> 00:36:08.060
Whoa, so big!

00:36:08.060 --> 00:36:09.390
It's almost overwhelming.

00:36:09.390 --> 00:36:11.060
It makes me want tea.

00:36:11.060 --> 00:36:12.480
This place is amazing!

00:36:12.480 --> 00:36:14.540
Let's go check our bags first.

00:36:14.540 --> 00:36:16.260
Good idea.

00:36:17.510 --> 00:36:19.140
We offer our sincerest apologies.

00:36:19.620 --> 00:36:22.910
We have a very full flight today,

00:36:22.910 --> 00:36:27.120
so we'll have to ask you to check those too.

00:36:31.410 --> 00:36:33.670
See you in London, Gitah!

00:36:34.020 --> 00:36:35.040
This thing's amazing!

00:36:35.040 --> 00:36:37.130
We should have one of these at school.

00:36:37.130 --> 00:36:38.500
A walking sidewalk!

00:36:38.500 --> 00:36:40.090
<i>Moving</i> sidewalk.

00:36:40.790 --> 00:36:42.800
I can see your legs!

00:36:43.180 --> 00:36:45.300
Is there truth behind this boyfriend rumor?!

00:36:45.300 --> 00:36:46.720
Are you really dating?!

00:36:47.090 --> 00:36:50.060
Put this to rest! Kotobuki-san!

00:36:52.060 --> 00:36:52.860
Moonwalk!

00:36:52.860 --> 00:36:54.060
Do the moonwalk!

00:36:54.420 --> 00:36:55.980
Quit playing around.

00:36:55.980 --> 00:36:57.230
Hey, look!

00:36:58.740 --> 00:37:00.250
Wow...

00:37:06.700 --> 00:37:07.580
Come on, Ritsu! Ritsu!

00:37:07.580 --> 00:37:08.610
Shouldn't we buy snacks?
Come on, Ritsu! Ritsu!

00:37:08.610 --> 00:37:09.380
Shouldn't we buy snacks?

00:37:09.380 --> 00:37:09.400
Oh, fine.
Shouldn't we buy snacks?

00:37:09.400 --> 00:37:10.380
They'll give us food on the plane.
Oh, fine.

00:37:10.380 --> 00:37:11.250
They'll give us food on the plane.

00:37:11.250 --> 00:37:11.740
You're so prepared, Azusa-chan.

00:37:11.740 --> 00:37:12.760
Rabbit ears!
You're so prepared, Azusa-chan.

00:37:12.760 --> 00:37:13.410
You're so prepared, Azusa-chan.

00:37:13.410 --> 00:37:15.710
I-I did some research.

00:37:18.430 --> 00:37:20.840
This is so unreal.

00:37:21.180 --> 00:37:24.760
We're boarding a plane that'll take us to London.

00:37:24.760 --> 00:37:26.800
We'll get off in a different country!

00:37:27.210 --> 00:37:29.930
It just hit me that we're really going overseas together!

00:37:30.290 --> 00:37:33.270
We might even end up traveling to the past. Or even the future!

00:37:33.270 --> 00:37:35.520
This isn't a time machine.

00:37:36.060 --> 00:37:38.020
But time will turn back.

00:37:38.020 --> 00:37:39.900
Whoa, Mugi-senpai!

00:37:41.210 --> 00:37:43.140
Here, your sleep masks.

00:37:43.140 --> 00:37:44.180
Oh, thank you.

00:37:44.180 --> 00:37:45.570
Thanks!

00:37:45.570 --> 00:37:46.090
Hey, Mugi. How do you use this?

00:37:46.090 --> 00:37:48.000
How's time gonna turn back?
Hey, Mugi. How do you use this?

00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:51.020
It's pretty simple, just press the button here.
It's because we're flying against the Earth's rotation.

00:37:51.020 --> 00:37:51.330
It's because we're flying against the Earth's rotation.

00:37:51.630 --> 00:37:54.300
And that makes time turn back?

00:37:54.300 --> 00:37:55.380
In a way.

00:37:55.380 --> 00:37:56.730
Okay, so—

00:37:58.840 --> 00:38:01.390
Fasten your seatbelt now.

00:38:01.390 --> 00:38:02.510
Got it.

00:38:04.120 --> 00:38:07.970
So if we kept going, would we end up in the past?

00:38:07.970 --> 00:38:10.100
It can't go back that far.

00:38:10.480 --> 00:38:11.700
So how far—

00:38:11.700 --> 00:38:13.530
Look, we're taking off.

00:38:14.020 --> 00:38:15.390
Takeoff?!

00:38:15.390 --> 00:38:17.900
Azu-nyan, we're moving!

00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:28.770
It's the clouds!

00:38:38.140 --> 00:38:41.250
No Japanese from here on out, Azu-nyan.

00:38:41.250 --> 00:38:41.880
What?

00:38:41.880 --> 00:38:43.370
Okay?

00:38:45.490 --> 00:38:47.180
I understand.

00:38:48.120 --> 00:38:49.680
Azu-cat!

00:38:51.410 --> 00:38:52.890
No Japanese!

00:38:52.890 --> 00:38:53.970
Fine.

00:38:55.810 --> 00:38:58.370
What's airline food called in English, Azu-cat?

00:38:58.370 --> 00:38:59.650
Flight meal.

00:38:59.980 --> 00:39:01.900
Chicken or beef?

00:39:03.320 --> 00:39:04.860
Exercise!

00:39:06.290 --> 00:39:08.090
Chicken, please.

00:39:08.090 --> 00:39:09.660
Excellent!

00:39:10.240 --> 00:39:12.590
And me? Me?

00:39:12.590 --> 00:39:14.580
Chicken or beef?
Cheers!

00:39:15.180 --> 00:39:16.800
Beef, please.

00:39:16.800 --> 00:39:18.160
Excellent!

00:39:18.160 --> 00:39:18.900
Excuse me, ma'am.

00:39:18.900 --> 00:39:19.540
Yes?

00:39:19.540 --> 00:39:22.500
Would you prefer the Japanese- or Western-style meal?

00:39:49.480 --> 00:39:51.500
Azu-nyan! Hey, Azu-nyan!

00:39:59.180 --> 00:40:00.360
Oh, yeah!

00:40:00.360 --> 00:40:02.610
I should think of lyrics for her song!

00:40:24.010 --> 00:40:27.050
Up we go!

00:40:35.280 --> 00:40:36.720
What's this?

00:40:37.400 --> 00:40:39.160
Worldwide?

00:40:43.860 --> 00:40:46.220
Did you see anything, Azu-nyan?

00:40:46.220 --> 00:40:48.090
No, not really.

00:40:51.600 --> 00:40:52.500
I see.

00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:54.680
Was something written on there?

00:40:55.100 --> 00:40:56.420
Yeah.

00:40:56.420 --> 00:40:58.890
Just a little bit about how I think I should live from now on.

00:41:00.560 --> 00:41:03.410
I have a lot to think about.

00:41:21.180 --> 00:41:22.700
<i>What was that?</i>

00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:29.550
<i>Is she really trying to change Afterschool Tea Time's image this late in the game?</i>

00:41:29.550 --> 00:41:34.550
<i>Or maybe she's really repeating a year and needs to think about her future.</i>

00:41:35.560 --> 00:41:39.620
<i>And she's thinking about becoming a wild, fanatical rocker.</i>

00:41:46.020 --> 00:41:47.400
Rise and shine, Azu-nyan!

00:41:48.780 --> 00:41:50.040
We're landing soon!

00:42:01.320 --> 00:42:02.300
Is this England?!

00:42:02.300 --> 00:42:04.480
Are we really in England?!

00:42:06.570 --> 00:42:08.530
The flight was over in the blink of an eye.

00:42:08.530 --> 00:42:09.800
This is so cool!

00:42:09.800 --> 00:42:10.790
We're foreigners!

00:42:10.790 --> 00:42:12.130
We flew through the sky!

00:42:12.130 --> 00:42:13.740
Calm down!

00:42:13.740 --> 00:42:15.360
We're really here...

00:42:15.360 --> 00:42:16.870
Next up is immigration, right?

00:42:16.870 --> 00:42:17.760
What do we do?

00:42:17.760 --> 00:42:18.840
Let's see.

00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:21.920
It says they usually ask the purpose of the trip.

00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:23.680
The purpose, huh?

00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:24.200
Yeah.

00:42:24.200 --> 00:42:27.190
Just say sightseeing, and you'll be fine.

00:42:27.190 --> 00:42:28.690
Okay!

00:42:28.690 --> 00:42:30.190
Side business!

00:42:30.190 --> 00:42:31.520
Side business?

00:42:31.520 --> 00:42:32.640
Hello!

00:42:32.640 --> 00:42:34.160
Y-Yes!

00:42:34.160 --> 00:42:35.140
Four days.

00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:39.030
Yes, I am 17.

00:42:44.540 --> 00:42:46.740
I missed you, Gitah!

00:42:46.740 --> 00:42:48.120
I feel so much better now.

00:42:48.120 --> 00:42:51.840
But when you stop and think about it,
why did we bring these?

00:42:51.840 --> 00:42:54.210
See your luggage yet, Mio?

00:42:54.210 --> 00:42:55.670
Not yet.

00:42:55.670 --> 00:42:56.670
Not yet?

00:42:56.670 --> 00:42:58.180
You'll see it soon.

00:42:58.180 --> 00:42:59.200
Yeah...

00:43:02.050 --> 00:43:04.520
Wow. It seriously didn't come out.

00:43:04.940 --> 00:43:07.230
Why just mine?

00:43:07.230 --> 00:43:09.210
You think they lost it?

00:43:09.210 --> 00:43:11.700
Whatever will you do without your panties, Akiyama-san?

00:43:11.700 --> 00:43:13.210
You're a lady!

00:43:13.210 --> 00:43:15.290
Mio-chan strips bare, remember?

00:43:15.290 --> 00:43:17.860
Yes! She is no panties!

00:43:17.860 --> 00:43:20.280
I told you, I meant that I don't wear socks to bed!

00:43:21.000 --> 00:43:22.120
It's right over there!

00:43:22.120 --> 00:43:23.740
Oh, you're right.

00:43:24.420 --> 00:43:26.700
Someone must've grabbed it by mistake.

00:43:26.700 --> 00:43:28.570
The darkest place is under the candlestick.

00:43:28.570 --> 00:43:30.370
Thank goodness!
All's well that ends well.

00:43:32.330 --> 00:43:33.290
Whoa, it's cold!

00:43:33.290 --> 00:43:35.640
London's pretty nippy.

00:43:36.640 --> 00:43:37.550
London's sky!

00:43:38.630 --> 00:43:40.460
A London taxi!

00:43:40.970 --> 00:43:43.050
London's English!

00:43:43.050 --> 00:43:45.570
Us in London!

00:43:46.330 --> 00:43:47.180
Enough.

00:43:48.030 --> 00:43:49.550
Taxi, taxi!

00:43:49.550 --> 00:43:50.850
Good afternoon.

00:43:50.850 --> 00:43:51.730
Hello.

00:43:51.730 --> 00:43:57.450
My dad told me that you have to
open taxi doors yourself in London.

00:43:57.450 --> 00:43:58.150
Really?

00:43:58.150 --> 00:44:00.280
Huh? There's no handle.

00:44:00.280 --> 00:44:02.740
Maybe it's automatic.

00:44:02.740 --> 00:44:03.620
Hey, Ricchan.

00:44:03.620 --> 00:44:04.730
You should ask—

00:44:06.170 --> 00:44:08.720
G-Got you, right? It's on the other side.

00:44:08.720 --> 00:44:10.420
Here, put your luggage up here in the front.

00:44:10.420 --> 00:44:11.870
Oh, thanks.

00:44:12.860 --> 00:44:13.790
Where are you going?

00:44:14.200 --> 00:44:15.560
We are, um...

00:44:15.560 --> 00:44:17.250
Hotel Ibis, please.

00:44:17.250 --> 00:44:18.700
Yeah, the Ibis!

00:44:18.700 --> 00:44:19.590
Which one?

00:44:20.050 --> 00:44:22.090
I think he's asking where it is.

00:44:22.440 --> 00:44:23.400
Where?

00:44:23.400 --> 00:44:25.930
In London, duh!

00:44:25.930 --> 00:44:27.220
Is this London's comedy?

00:44:27.580 --> 00:44:29.010
London City?

00:44:29.010 --> 00:44:30.350
Yes!

00:44:30.350 --> 00:44:31.810
We're sitting the wrong way!

00:44:31.810 --> 00:44:33.520
This feels kinda weird.

00:44:35.270 --> 00:44:37.930
H-Hey, are you okay?

00:44:37.930 --> 00:44:38.960
Sorry, Yui!

00:44:38.960 --> 00:44:41.110
I closed the door too quickly.

00:44:41.110 --> 00:44:42.960
It's okay. I'm fine.

00:44:42.960 --> 00:44:45.660
Mugi-chan's soft thighs broke my fall.

00:44:45.660 --> 00:44:46.580
That's good.

00:44:47.290 --> 00:44:48.420
Well, well.

00:44:48.420 --> 00:44:49.820
That was a shock.

00:44:49.820 --> 00:44:52.580
Yeah, you're telling me.

00:44:52.580 --> 00:44:54.780
Foreign countries are full of surprises.

00:45:07.050 --> 00:45:10.390
Lon-Lon-Lon-do-don!

00:45:13.850 --> 00:45:16.070
Thank you!

00:45:17.250 --> 00:45:21.020
I guess riding in the cab like that was a little hard on me.

00:45:21.020 --> 00:45:22.580
Are you okay, Yui-chan?

00:45:22.580 --> 00:45:24.240
I'm perfectly fine!

00:45:24.800 --> 00:45:27.120
Can we sit down for a bit?

00:45:29.120 --> 00:45:30.540
You sure you're all right?

00:45:31.220 --> 00:45:32.790
Can you hold down dinner?

00:45:32.790 --> 00:45:34.670
Dinner?

00:45:34.670 --> 00:45:37.480
I wanna eat roast beef.

00:45:37.480 --> 00:45:38.590
And ice cream!

00:45:39.440 --> 00:45:41.260
Oh no!

00:45:41.260 --> 00:45:42.050
What's wrong?

00:45:43.110 --> 00:45:45.550
We don't have a reservation here.

00:45:45.550 --> 00:45:47.660
So we can't stay here?

00:45:47.660 --> 00:45:49.170
Are we stuck on the streets?!

00:45:49.850 --> 00:45:51.280
What now?

00:45:51.280 --> 00:45:52.680
May I see that?

00:45:53.060 --> 00:45:54.520
Y-Yes!

00:45:58.660 --> 00:46:01.650
You've reserved the Ibis Earl's Court.

00:46:02.150 --> 00:46:03.820
Earl's Court?

00:46:03.820 --> 00:46:04.820
Yes.

00:46:04.820 --> 00:46:07.320
This is the Ibis London City.

00:46:07.320 --> 00:46:09.740
We have many locations throughout London.

00:46:09.740 --> 00:46:11.030
What's she saying, Mugi-senpai?

00:46:12.250 --> 00:46:13.120
She's too fast.

00:46:14.420 --> 00:46:15.830
She's saying...

00:46:15.830 --> 00:46:17.500
that they have more than one location.

00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:18.880
Really?

00:46:18.880 --> 00:46:23.410
And that our reservation is at the Earl's Court location.

00:46:23.410 --> 00:46:25.470
Seriously? That's a relief...

00:46:25.470 --> 00:46:26.700
Okay!

00:46:26.700 --> 00:46:27.630
Thank you desu!

00:46:27.630 --> 00:46:28.880
You're welcome.

00:46:28.880 --> 00:46:30.140
Have a nice day!

00:46:31.420 --> 00:46:33.880
Okay... Where's Earl's Court?

00:46:33.880 --> 00:46:34.820
Found it!

00:46:34.820 --> 00:46:36.370
It's right here.

00:46:36.370 --> 00:46:38.150
And we're here right now.

00:46:38.150 --> 00:46:40.380
It's pretty far away.

00:46:40.380 --> 00:46:41.970
Should we take a taxi again?

00:46:41.970 --> 00:46:44.280
You wanna see Yui fly again?

00:46:44.280 --> 00:46:46.530
I want to sit on the other side this time!

00:46:46.530 --> 00:46:49.380
Hey, why don't we take a bus?

00:46:49.380 --> 00:46:50.950
Good idea!

00:46:50.950 --> 00:46:52.370
Let's see...

00:46:53.170 --> 00:46:55.500
Can you read it, Mio-senpai?

00:46:55.500 --> 00:46:58.060
I don't see a direct route.

00:46:58.060 --> 00:46:59.660
Oh well.

00:46:59.660 --> 00:47:03.010
Oh, looks like the subway will take us straight there.

00:47:04.540 --> 00:47:06.130
What's wrong, Azu-nyan?

00:47:06.580 --> 00:47:10.810
Well, I'm wearing new shoes...

00:47:10.810 --> 00:47:12.820
Do your feet hurt?

00:47:12.820 --> 00:47:13.700
A little.

00:47:13.700 --> 00:47:15.060
Got a blister?

00:47:15.060 --> 00:47:16.720
How long have they been hurting?

00:47:16.720 --> 00:47:19.770
It just started a bit ago.

00:47:20.480 --> 00:47:23.610
Let's go buy you new shoes, then!

00:47:23.610 --> 00:47:26.380
No, it's fine! You must all be tired!

00:47:26.380 --> 00:47:27.740
And we still have our luggage!

00:47:27.740 --> 00:47:30.070
How about we go here, then?

00:47:30.070 --> 00:47:31.180
Where? Show me!

00:47:31.180 --> 00:47:31.880
Here.

00:47:31.880 --> 00:47:34.130
Apparently they sell punk clothing here.

00:47:34.130 --> 00:47:35.300
Wow!

00:47:35.300 --> 00:47:36.850
Sound good, Azusa?

00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:54.890
Azu-nyan, we're moving!

00:48:00.520 --> 00:48:02.270
Everything looks so cool!

00:48:03.580 --> 00:48:05.320
I gotta take a picture with Gitah!

00:48:08.560 --> 00:48:11.300
I <i>azu</i>ssure I <i>cat</i> help you with that, Yui-chan.

00:48:12.730 --> 00:48:14.570
How are they, Azu-nyan?

00:48:14.570 --> 00:48:16.680
You should be good now.

00:48:16.680 --> 00:48:18.910
Yeah, these are much better.

00:48:18.910 --> 00:48:20.300
That's good.

00:48:20.300 --> 00:48:22.700
They look great on you, Azu-nyan!

00:48:24.090 --> 00:48:25.340
Hey, look over there!

00:48:25.810 --> 00:48:26.920
Sushi!

00:48:26.920 --> 00:48:28.940
It's a sushi-go-round bar.

00:48:28.940 --> 00:48:30.220
It spins?

00:48:30.220 --> 00:48:30.760
Yeah.

00:48:32.200 --> 00:48:34.240
You've never been to one before, Mugi?

00:48:34.240 --> 00:48:36.080
Really? Let's go, then!

00:48:36.080 --> 00:48:37.570
Even though we're in London?

00:48:37.570 --> 00:48:39.890
No, <i>because</i> we're in London.

00:48:40.380 --> 00:48:43.130
Let's see what you're made of...

00:48:43.130 --> 00:48:44.640
London!

00:48:47.590 --> 00:48:48.360
What's this?

00:48:50.920 --> 00:48:52.450
What's going on in here?

00:48:52.860 --> 00:48:54.820
It has a real fancy vibe to it.

00:48:56.470 --> 00:48:57.890
It's spinning!

00:48:57.890 --> 00:48:59.410
It's spinning...

00:48:59.410 --> 00:49:01.640
I'm getting chills just looking at it.

00:49:01.640 --> 00:49:03.920
Trauma from the airport resurfacing?

00:49:04.530 --> 00:49:07.530
But this isn't exactly what I thought it'd be.

00:49:07.530 --> 00:49:11.010
I imagined the sushi twirling around like ballerinas.

00:49:11.010 --> 00:49:12.500
Looks like they have a stage—

00:49:12.500 --> 00:49:13.260
Hello.

00:49:14.420 --> 00:49:16.680
You're the ones from Japan, right?

00:49:18.130 --> 00:49:22.520
I heard "from" and "Japan," so...

00:49:23.220 --> 00:49:24.690
Y-Yes.

00:49:25.050 --> 00:49:27.750
I'm the manager of this establishment.

00:49:27.750 --> 00:49:31.070
You're the ones who will be performing today, correct?

00:49:31.070 --> 00:49:34.220
U-Um...

00:49:34.220 --> 00:49:34.840
Yes.

00:49:34.840 --> 00:49:36.090
So tall!

00:49:36.090 --> 00:49:38.010
Welcome to my sushi bar!

00:49:38.010 --> 00:49:39.530
Yes!

00:49:39.530 --> 00:49:42.340
You're too quick to say "yes" to everything.

00:49:42.340 --> 00:49:44.870
But he's welcoming us.

00:49:44.870 --> 00:49:46.400
This way, please!

00:49:46.400 --> 00:49:48.080
Yes!

00:49:52.960 --> 00:49:57.240
Wow, so you wear happi whenever you eat at sushi bars in London!

00:49:57.240 --> 00:50:00.190
Reminds me of the aprons they wear in barbecue restaurants.

00:50:01.350 --> 00:50:04.450
Okay, if you'd like to get on stage!

00:50:09.470 --> 00:50:10.360
Gitah!

00:50:10.360 --> 00:50:12.360
What's going on?

00:50:12.360 --> 00:50:13.440
Really now?!

00:50:13.440 --> 00:50:14.370
Mugi-chan?

00:50:14.370 --> 00:50:15.460
Mugi!

00:50:18.580 --> 00:50:20.330
Excuse me!

00:50:24.770 --> 00:50:30.050
I'm sure she's telling them that we're only here to eat sushi.

00:50:30.050 --> 00:50:32.960
It's good to have Mugi around at times like the—

00:50:32.960 --> 00:50:33.960
I take it back!

00:50:37.590 --> 00:50:39.840
Why'd you do that, Mugi?

00:50:39.840 --> 00:50:41.810
I didn't bring my keyboard.

00:50:41.810 --> 00:50:44.090
It's all on me, then!

00:50:44.090 --> 00:50:45.020
Hey, you!

00:50:45.020 --> 00:50:46.860
I'm our leader
<i>I am buchou!</i>

00:50:46.860 --> 00:50:49.840
We're just customers
<i>We are okyakusan.</i>

00:50:49.840 --> 00:50:51.760
We're not here to play
<i>Ensou shimasen.</i>

00:50:51.760 --> 00:50:55.140
Ricchan! I know you're trying,
but that's way too much Japanese!

00:50:55.640 --> 00:50:58.200
Try again, Ricchan!

00:50:58.200 --> 00:51:00.340
I-I...

00:51:02.700 --> 00:51:04.620
I love sushi.

00:51:05.660 --> 00:51:07.870
London's something else, that's for sure.

00:51:08.710 --> 00:51:11.630
He's staring right at us, Ricchan.

00:51:11.630 --> 00:51:14.630
We really can't get out of this now.

00:51:15.090 --> 00:51:18.440
We'll just have to play something, then.

00:51:18.440 --> 00:51:19.480
Yeah.

00:51:19.480 --> 00:51:22.750
They might not let us eat if we don't.

00:51:22.750 --> 00:51:26.100
We have to play something just to eat?!

00:51:26.100 --> 00:51:27.180
What should we play?

00:51:27.180 --> 00:51:28.900
What song, Yui?

00:51:30.720 --> 00:51:32.270
Um...

00:51:32.970 --> 00:51:35.090
Um...

00:51:39.320 --> 00:51:40.910
Curry Before Rice!

00:51:41.250 --> 00:51:42.480
At a sushi bar?!

00:51:42.480 --> 00:51:44.540
I mean, they both have rice.

00:51:46.680 --> 00:51:49.700
And he looks like a good person.

00:51:58.760 --> 00:51:59.970
Let's do this!

00:51:59.970 --> 00:52:01.670
Who are you supposed to be?

00:52:01.670 --> 00:52:03.340
Don't leave us in the dark.

00:52:04.600 --> 00:52:05.780
Sorry, sorry!

00:52:05.780 --> 00:52:08.010
I got too psyched up!

00:52:09.230 --> 00:52:11.900
W-We should hurry up and start soon!

00:52:13.270 --> 00:52:16.630
A-Azu-nyan, you sound off by half a semitone!

00:52:16.630 --> 00:52:18.780
Tuning takes too much time!

00:52:19.280 --> 00:52:20.860
I'll just match your sound!

00:52:43.200 --> 00:52:44.970
One, two! One, two, three, four!

00:52:49.960 --> 00:52:52.190
Hello! We're Afternoon Tea Time!

00:53:55.290 --> 00:53:56.230
Thank you!

00:53:56.230 --> 00:53:58.420
<i>Arigatou gozaimashita!</i>

00:53:58.420 --> 00:53:59.630
Wonderful!

00:53:59.630 --> 00:54:00.710
That's a nice one!

00:54:00.710 --> 00:54:02.230
Rice!

00:54:02.230 --> 00:54:04.070
Thank you, thank you!

00:54:04.070 --> 00:54:06.150
So about the sushi...

00:54:06.150 --> 00:54:09.320
Thank you, Love Crisis!

00:54:10.100 --> 00:54:13.880
What was that last thing he said?

00:54:13.880 --> 00:54:16.860
He said "Love Crisis," didn't he?

00:54:17.780 --> 00:54:20.490
Where have I heard that name before?

00:54:20.490 --> 00:54:22.830
That's Ricchan's friend's band!

00:54:22.830 --> 00:54:24.130
Yeah.

00:54:25.100 --> 00:54:29.780
I guess your friend's band is Love Crisis Japan, then.

00:54:30.490 --> 00:54:33.700
Spinning things never end well.

00:54:34.210 --> 00:54:36.010
And you know...

00:54:36.010 --> 00:54:39.290
I'm so hungry!

00:54:39.290 --> 00:54:40.540
Thanks for reminding me.

00:54:40.540 --> 00:54:41.920
She just had to say it.

00:54:41.920 --> 00:54:43.870
I wanna...

00:54:43.870 --> 00:54:45.630
...eat sushi!

00:54:45.630 --> 00:54:49.200
I can't bring myself to go back in there, though.

00:54:50.180 --> 00:54:54.700
You think everyone in there had to play before they got to eat?

00:54:56.270 --> 00:54:59.220
Well, we're blocking the entrance, so let's hit the road.

00:54:59.220 --> 00:55:00.380
I guess we should.

00:55:00.680 --> 00:55:04.050
But seriously, what was wrong with that sushi bar?

00:55:04.050 --> 00:55:04.760
Whoa!

00:55:04.760 --> 00:55:06.240
Ricchan! Mio-chan!

00:55:06.240 --> 00:55:07.320
Yes!

00:55:07.320 --> 00:55:08.900
Never thought I'd see you here!

00:55:08.900 --> 00:55:09.840
You traveling?

00:55:09.840 --> 00:55:10.680
Yes!

00:55:10.680 --> 00:55:12.650
Sightseeing!

00:55:12.650 --> 00:55:13.660
The whole group's here!

00:55:13.660 --> 00:55:14.790
Yes!

00:55:16.490 --> 00:55:19.000
Wow, I'm a natural genius at English!

00:55:19.000 --> 00:55:21.300
But they're speaking Japanese...

00:55:22.460 --> 00:55:23.890
Maki-chan?!

00:55:23.890 --> 00:55:25.630
Love Crisis Japan!

00:55:26.740 --> 00:55:28.160
Why <i>here</i>? Why <i>now</i>?

00:55:28.160 --> 00:55:29.910
Why are <i>you</i> here?

00:55:29.910 --> 00:55:32.690
I don't get it!

00:55:33.180 --> 00:55:34.350
What's wrong?

00:55:34.350 --> 00:55:38.100
We just wanted sushi, but they made us play!

00:55:38.100 --> 00:55:41.400
And so we did, but they didn't even let us eat!

00:55:41.400 --> 00:55:43.180
We must've sucked pretty bad!

00:55:43.180 --> 00:55:44.880
Really?

00:55:44.880 --> 00:55:49.140
We're supposed to play here
to celebrate the shop's opening.

00:55:49.140 --> 00:55:53.280
I know! They must've mistaken us for Love Crisis!

00:55:53.280 --> 00:55:55.170
You cracked that case, Mugi-chan!

00:55:55.650 --> 00:55:57.770
Remember Kawakami-san?

00:55:57.770 --> 00:55:59.000
From the music club?

00:55:59.000 --> 00:55:59.860
Yeah.

00:55:59.860 --> 00:56:02.540
She set us up with this bar.

00:56:02.540 --> 00:56:05.210
She knows the manager of this place.

00:56:06.700 --> 00:56:09.780
Wow, it's a small world sometimes.

00:56:09.780 --> 00:56:11.590
Really makes you think.

00:56:11.590 --> 00:56:13.420
Oh, sorry!

00:56:13.420 --> 00:56:15.750
They think you've already played now!

00:56:15.750 --> 00:56:17.120
I guess you're right.

00:56:17.120 --> 00:56:18.420
We'll go talk to them.

00:56:18.420 --> 00:56:19.870
Okay! Later!

00:56:19.870 --> 00:56:20.590
See you!

00:56:20.590 --> 00:56:21.310
Bye-bye!

00:56:22.220 --> 00:56:24.360
They're pretty cool...

00:56:24.780 --> 00:56:26.270
Yeah...

00:56:29.170 --> 00:56:32.130
We're finally checked in.

00:56:33.080 --> 00:56:36.860
We're finally alone together, Azu-nyan!

00:56:36.860 --> 00:56:37.820
Yeah.

00:56:37.820 --> 00:56:39.370
It's been a long day.

00:56:39.370 --> 00:56:41.400
I'm hungry...

00:56:41.400 --> 00:56:43.780
I wanna take a bath...

00:56:43.780 --> 00:56:46.590
I can't blame you. It was pretty cold out there.

00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:52.090
What are we gonna do about dinner?

00:56:54.400 --> 00:56:55.720
After all that, this is our dinner?

00:56:57.180 --> 00:56:58.740
Thank you, Ui-chan!

00:56:59.530 --> 00:57:01.840
We'll have to thank her once we get back.

00:57:01.840 --> 00:57:05.250
We can't eat these without a microwave, though!

00:57:06.300 --> 00:57:09.170
What were you three doing in here before this?

00:57:09.170 --> 00:57:10.860
Taking pictures!

00:57:10.860 --> 00:57:11.830
In your school uniforms?

00:57:11.830 --> 00:57:14.490
That's why we brought them in the first place!

00:57:14.490 --> 00:57:16.870
You're way too easily excited!

00:57:16.870 --> 00:57:19.830
I see you changed into yours too, Mio-senpai.

00:57:19.830 --> 00:57:21.750
Phew, that felt good.

00:57:22.260 --> 00:57:24.710
Ui's prepared for anything.

00:57:24.710 --> 00:57:27.210
That's my little Ui!

00:57:29.320 --> 00:57:30.000
Are you okay?!

00:57:30.890 --> 00:57:32.590
It shot fire at me...

00:57:32.590 --> 00:57:33.290
Scary!

00:57:33.290 --> 00:57:35.270
You need to use a transformer, Yui-chan.

00:57:35.620 --> 00:57:39.200
I don't wanna... I'm too scared...

00:57:40.020 --> 00:57:41.730
Let's just eat.

00:57:46.480 --> 00:57:49.020
I'm repeating a year, Azu-nyan!

00:57:49.730 --> 00:57:52.060
We're classmates now!

00:57:52.060 --> 00:57:52.900
What?!

00:57:52.900 --> 00:57:53.990
Let's do our best this year!

00:57:53.990 --> 00:57:57.280
What should I call you now, Yui-senpai?

00:57:57.280 --> 00:58:00.410
Just call me Yui.

00:58:00.410 --> 00:58:01.410
Yui?

00:58:01.410 --> 00:58:02.250
Yeah.

00:58:02.910 --> 00:58:04.410
Yu... i?

00:58:04.410 --> 00:58:06.170
Louder!

00:58:06.810 --> 00:58:08.890
Stop that, Yui!

00:58:08.890 --> 00:58:10.000
Just like that.

00:58:10.360 --> 00:58:11.800
It just doesn't feel right!

00:58:11.800 --> 00:58:15.940
But we're in the same grade now.

00:58:15.940 --> 00:58:17.880
Same grade now...

00:58:17.880 --> 00:58:19.220
Same grade now...

00:58:36.860 --> 00:58:38.110
<i>What's that?</i>

00:58:38.650 --> 00:58:41.530
<i>That's so creepy, Yui-senpai!</i>

00:58:46.510 --> 00:58:48.440
Good night.

01:00:25.470 --> 01:00:27.960
Phew, I needed that.

01:00:27.960 --> 01:00:29.170
Yeah.

01:00:29.180 --> 01:00:33.280
Hey, there's something I wanted to see while we're already here.

01:00:33.280 --> 01:00:35.940
You used it in your play at the school festival.

01:00:35.940 --> 01:00:37.620
Ricchan's tombstone!

01:00:37.620 --> 01:00:38.080
Yeah!

01:00:38.080 --> 01:00:38.780
Hey.

01:00:38.780 --> 01:00:42.280
The occult club made a pretty accurate look-alike.

01:00:42.280 --> 01:00:43.450
They're so passionate.

01:00:43.450 --> 01:00:44.990
This is also a replica, though.

01:00:45.320 --> 01:00:47.300
We've walked so much today!

01:00:47.300 --> 01:00:49.020
Let's find somewhere to rest.

01:00:49.020 --> 01:00:52.320
I think there's a place nearby where we can have afternoon tea.

01:00:52.320 --> 01:00:53.790
Afternoon tea?!

01:00:53.790 --> 01:00:56.750
That's our heart and soul, Azu-nyan!

01:00:57.370 --> 01:01:00.170
I can't believe we needed a reservation...

01:01:12.320 --> 01:01:14.190
It's huge!

01:01:14.550 --> 01:01:16.360
It's spinning...

01:01:17.640 --> 01:01:18.610
It's spinning!

01:01:19.210 --> 01:01:21.070
Let's go ride it together!

01:01:21.070 --> 01:01:22.850
You're coming, right, Mugi-chan?

01:01:22.850 --> 01:01:23.900
Right, Mio-chan?

01:01:24.510 --> 01:01:28.570
I-I'll stay down here and watch our stuff!

01:01:29.570 --> 01:01:31.770
See you! Enjoy yourselves!

01:01:32.960 --> 01:01:33.660
Mio...

01:01:33.660 --> 01:01:34.470
Mio-chan...

01:01:34.470 --> 01:01:36.210
Oh, come on. Just do it!

01:01:36.210 --> 01:01:38.880
I don't wanna! No more spinning things!

01:01:38.880 --> 01:01:41.420
You'll be fine! We're all here for you.

01:01:41.420 --> 01:01:42.720
You can do it, Mio-chan!

01:01:42.720 --> 01:01:44.090
No more spinning!

01:01:44.090 --> 01:01:45.790
Wow!

01:01:45.790 --> 01:01:47.890
You can see all of London from up here!

01:01:47.890 --> 01:01:48.300
Hey, Azusa! Look at that!

01:01:48.300 --> 01:01:49.720
Mio-chan's sure having fun.
Hey, Azusa! Look at that!

01:01:49.720 --> 01:01:50.480
Mio-chan's sure having fun.

01:01:50.480 --> 01:01:53.770
You kind of forget it's spinning in circles while you're on it.

01:01:53.770 --> 01:01:56.020
Just wow!

01:01:56.640 --> 01:01:57.820
Let's take pictures!

01:01:59.680 --> 01:02:02.230
I <i>azu</i>ssure you I <i>cat</i> help with that, Mio!

01:02:04.130 --> 01:02:05.980
God, there's loads of people here today.

01:02:05.990 --> 01:02:08.240
Do you see what I see, Ricchan?

01:02:12.490 --> 01:02:13.420
Mugi!

01:02:13.420 --> 01:02:15.570
I need your <i>azu</i>ssurance that
you <i>cat</i> keep this safe for me.

01:02:15.570 --> 01:02:16.560
Okay!

01:02:16.560 --> 01:02:17.930
It's catching on!

01:02:19.920 --> 01:02:21.050
Later!

01:02:21.050 --> 01:02:22.160
See you!

01:02:22.160 --> 01:02:23.550
I'll see you tomorr—

01:02:23.550 --> 01:02:25.050
Our room's right here, though.

01:02:27.930 --> 01:02:30.180
I'm home!

01:02:37.810 --> 01:02:40.330
I'm sorry! Are you okay?

01:02:40.330 --> 01:02:42.730
But I...

01:02:42.730 --> 01:02:44.680
I don't swing that way!

01:02:44.680 --> 01:02:46.490
What's that mean?

01:02:46.490 --> 01:02:50.700
I just wanted to hug Gitah...

01:02:53.700 --> 01:02:55.700
I'm sorry! I misunderstood!

01:02:55.700 --> 01:02:57.050
I'm so sorry!

01:02:57.970 --> 01:02:59.820
I-It's fine...

01:02:59.820 --> 01:03:04.000
I'm glad the self-defense book that Ui gave us came in handy.

01:03:05.690 --> 01:03:07.010
Are you going to sleep, Azu-nyan?

01:03:07.700 --> 01:03:13.010
Want me to sing you a lullaby?

01:03:14.150 --> 01:03:16.300
Sleep, sleep...

01:03:16.300 --> 01:03:16.650
Go to sleep... Go to sleep, little baby...

01:03:16.650 --> 01:03:18.410
I'm sorry.
Go to sleep... Go to sleep, little baby...

01:03:18.410 --> 01:03:23.500
Go to sleep... Go to sleep, little baby...

01:03:33.700 --> 01:03:38.190
Wait! We're not here to look at pictures!

01:03:38.190 --> 01:03:42.040
Did anyone come up with a theme to get Azusa-chan's song started?

01:03:42.420 --> 01:03:44.380
Not a single one.

01:03:44.380 --> 01:03:50.400
I thought that we'd get some kind of super idea while in London.

01:03:52.300 --> 01:03:56.410
Big Ben! London Eye! River Thames!

01:03:56.410 --> 01:03:57.640
You know, like that!

01:03:57.640 --> 01:04:01.440
You're just listing famous places while projecting your voice.

01:04:01.440 --> 01:04:05.320
I wanna make a song greater than anything we've ever done before!

01:04:05.850 --> 01:04:11.660
Something that'll inspire her long after we're gone!

01:04:11.660 --> 01:04:13.570
A song that'll make her feel invincible!

01:04:13.570 --> 01:04:15.580
Invincible, huh?

01:04:19.830 --> 01:04:21.220
What's up?

01:04:22.720 --> 01:04:26.540
I just realized I forgot my room key.

01:04:28.350 --> 01:04:30.880
Can't you get back through there?

01:04:43.360 --> 01:04:47.090
It really is a trail this time...

01:04:47.820 --> 01:04:51.610
Well, I'll be going back to Azu-nyan now.

01:04:51.610 --> 01:04:54.030
You dropped some candies.

01:04:54.030 --> 01:04:56.760
They're all yours. Dig in.

01:04:56.760 --> 01:04:58.050
Good night, Yui-chan.

01:04:58.050 --> 01:04:59.390
Good night!

01:04:59.390 --> 01:05:01.270
She's so easygoing.

01:05:02.960 --> 01:05:05.680
Who might it be at this hour?

01:05:05.680 --> 01:05:07.660
It's too high...

01:05:12.050 --> 01:05:14.300
Hide everything! It's Azusa!

01:05:14.300 --> 01:05:15.700
Coming!

01:05:15.700 --> 01:05:16.720
Come on in!

01:05:16.720 --> 01:05:18.060
Oh, thanks.

01:05:18.060 --> 01:05:19.380
Azusa-chan!

01:05:19.380 --> 01:05:20.880
What brings you here?

01:05:29.460 --> 01:05:32.100
Sorry to bother you.

01:05:43.040 --> 01:05:44.820
We've got a problem, Ricchan!

01:05:44.850 --> 01:05:46.240
What'll we do?!

01:05:46.240 --> 01:05:47.480
Calm down, Yui.

01:05:47.480 --> 01:05:48.540
Azu-nyan's missing!

01:05:48.540 --> 01:05:49.750
She was just here.

01:05:50.810 --> 01:05:52.050
She already went back, though.

01:05:52.050 --> 01:05:53.260
Really?

01:05:59.680 --> 01:06:01.180
Something's going on, Ritsu-senpai!

01:06:01.410 --> 01:06:02.310
Oh, she's awake now.

01:06:02.770 --> 01:06:04.070
Yui-senpai's nowhere to be found!

01:06:07.840 --> 01:06:09.680
She wasn't there, Ricchan!

01:06:09.680 --> 01:06:11.230
We have to find her!

01:06:11.230 --> 01:06:13.690
This is no joke, Azu-nyan!

01:06:13.690 --> 01:06:15.320
You're missing!

01:06:16.840 --> 01:06:17.850
You're here!

01:06:17.850 --> 01:06:18.410
Right...

01:06:18.840 --> 01:06:22.370
Where were you?! I was worried sick!

01:06:22.370 --> 01:06:23.410
Um...

01:06:25.360 --> 01:06:26.290
The phone's ringing!

01:06:26.290 --> 01:06:27.670
Who's calling?

01:06:27.670 --> 01:06:28.950
The front desk?

01:06:28.950 --> 01:06:30.170
This late at night?

01:06:30.170 --> 01:06:32.090
Maybe it's from Japan?

01:06:32.090 --> 01:06:34.800
It's six in the morning in Japan right now.

01:06:34.800 --> 01:06:37.760
You've got the time difference down, Yui-chan.

01:06:39.170 --> 01:06:39.540
<i>Hai?</i>

01:06:39.540 --> 01:06:40.280
I mean...

01:06:40.280 --> 01:06:41.220
Hello?

01:06:41.220 --> 01:06:44.420
Yes! O-Oh, yes!

01:06:44.420 --> 01:06:46.270
What?! A murder?!

01:06:46.270 --> 01:06:47.520
Just kidding!

01:06:47.520 --> 01:06:49.610
They hung up before I could answer!

01:06:50.360 --> 01:06:50.760
You're lucky I didn't bite my tongue there!

01:06:50.760 --> 01:06:52.860
I wonder who it was.
You're lucky I didn't bite my tongue there!

01:06:52.860 --> 01:06:56.360
They'll call back if it was important.

01:06:56.360 --> 01:06:58.110
I guess so.

01:07:01.700 --> 01:07:03.940
<i>A song that'll make her feel invincible...</i>

01:07:10.480 --> 01:07:13.890
What should I call you now, Yui-senpai?

01:07:13.890 --> 01:07:15.380
Azu-nyan?

01:07:17.710 --> 01:07:19.450
I guess it was just sleep talk.

01:07:23.920 --> 01:07:24.840
You know,

01:07:24.840 --> 01:07:27.850
you should blink every once in a while.

01:07:28.420 --> 01:07:30.600
<i>A song for Azu-nyan...</i>

01:07:31.220 --> 01:07:32.310
Hello?

01:07:32.310 --> 01:07:33.920
<i>Azu-nyan, nyan, nyan...</i>

01:07:33.920 --> 01:07:35.190
<i>Azu-nyan, nyan, nyan!</i>

01:07:35.190 --> 01:07:37.650
Stop staring at me already!

01:07:37.650 --> 01:07:38.940
Seriously...

01:07:40.120 --> 01:07:42.030
<i>She got mad at me.</i>

01:07:43.620 --> 01:07:47.580
I can't think of anything to get her song started.

01:07:48.130 --> 01:07:49.600
<i>Azu-nyan, nyan, nyan...</i>

01:07:49.600 --> 01:07:51.540
<i>Azu-nyan, nyan, nyan!</i>

01:07:52.050 --> 01:07:54.670
<i>I won't get anywhere with that stuck in my head.</i>

01:07:56.650 --> 01:07:58.760
<i>London, London...</i>

01:07:59.170 --> 01:08:00.720
Recycling only!

01:08:01.230 --> 01:08:02.470
<i>Focus!</i>

01:08:04.090 --> 01:08:05.850
Yui-senpai!

01:08:07.740 --> 01:08:09.680
It's time to get going!

01:08:09.680 --> 01:08:11.150
Azu-nyan!

01:08:12.060 --> 01:08:12.800
Whoa!

01:08:17.740 --> 01:08:19.700
That's totally London!

01:08:19.700 --> 01:08:22.280
It's Yui-senpai's guitar!

01:08:22.280 --> 01:08:23.690
You're right!

01:08:24.320 --> 01:08:26.580
<i>A song for Azu-nyan...</i>

01:08:26.580 --> 01:08:28.790
<i>It needs to be something super big!</i>

01:08:29.120 --> 01:08:33.130
<i>Big, big, super big...</i>

01:08:33.130 --> 01:08:34.380
<i>Stay focused!</i>

01:08:38.800 --> 01:08:41.300
<i>A song for Azu-nyan...</i>

01:08:47.160 --> 01:08:50.920
<i>A song as cool as London...</i>

01:08:54.560 --> 01:08:56.980
That's rare. It's from Kawakami-san.

01:09:00.280 --> 01:09:01.320
News travels fast.

01:09:01.830 --> 01:09:02.820
How's it going?

01:09:02.820 --> 01:09:04.890
Let me on next!

01:09:05.730 --> 01:09:09.530
I heard from Maki-chan that you're all in London right now too.

01:09:09.530 --> 01:09:10.660
<i>Yeah, we are.</i>

01:09:10.660 --> 01:09:13.540
Mind doing me a favor?

01:09:14.460 --> 01:09:18.570
<i>There's this event going on nearby to promote Japanese pop culture.</i>

01:09:19.050 --> 01:09:22.050
<i>Love Crisis and Black Frill are both playing.</i>

01:09:22.520 --> 01:09:24.930
<i>Do you guys think you can play too?</i>

01:09:26.610 --> 01:09:27.730
Popcorn?

01:09:27.730 --> 01:09:28.860
No.

01:09:28.860 --> 01:09:31.470
It's tomorrow afternoon. Will you still be there?

01:09:31.470 --> 01:09:32.020
Yeah.

01:09:32.360 --> 01:09:35.380
I'll text you all the details later.

01:09:40.050 --> 01:09:43.620
They want to sell us as a high school girls' band.

01:09:43.620 --> 01:09:44.750
Hey, I was wondering...

01:09:45.240 --> 01:09:47.600
If someone texts us from Japan,

01:09:47.600 --> 01:09:50.410
was that message sent to the past?

01:09:50.410 --> 01:09:51.920
Of course not.

01:09:51.920 --> 01:09:56.940
But while it's still today here,
it's already tomorrow in Japan.

01:09:56.940 --> 01:09:57.830
That's because...

01:09:58.840 --> 01:10:00.440
What do you think we should do?

01:10:00.440 --> 01:10:02.350
It's a little out of the blue.

01:10:02.350 --> 01:10:07.190
That also means we send messages to the future!

01:10:07.190 --> 01:10:10.240
Yui-senpai, you're just sidetracking the conversation.

01:10:10.240 --> 01:10:11.430
Please keep quiet for now.

01:10:11.430 --> 01:10:13.270
So should we decline?

01:10:13.660 --> 01:10:15.560
I wanna play.

01:10:17.230 --> 01:10:18.440
Don't you?

01:10:18.440 --> 01:10:22.110
I don't know about you, but I think this is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

01:10:22.460 --> 01:10:23.440
We can do it!

01:10:23.440 --> 01:10:26.700
It won't end up like the sushi bar again!

01:10:27.130 --> 01:10:29.620
That's not really the problem here.

01:10:30.020 --> 01:10:31.820
I want to do it too!

01:10:32.990 --> 01:10:33.820
That's that, then.

01:10:33.820 --> 01:10:35.790
I'll send a reply to Kawakami-san.

01:10:44.880 --> 01:10:46.800
Come on! You too, Azu-nyan!

01:10:48.780 --> 01:10:49.300
Okay!

01:10:51.320 --> 01:10:52.960
All right! And...

01:10:52.960 --> 01:10:53.970
send!

01:10:55.270 --> 01:10:57.800
We sent it to the future!

01:10:58.590 --> 01:10:59.400
There's one problem...

01:11:00.650 --> 01:11:02.820
We fly back tomorrow.

01:11:03.170 --> 01:11:04.570
Oh, that's right.

01:11:04.570 --> 01:11:07.110
Will we catch our flight in time?

01:11:09.080 --> 01:11:10.820
What time was our flight?

01:11:10.820 --> 01:11:12.910
We should be at the airport by five.

01:11:13.730 --> 01:11:15.650
We start playing at four.

01:11:15.650 --> 01:11:17.300
Don't worry about it!

01:11:17.870 --> 01:11:19.310
We'll make it!

01:11:19.310 --> 01:11:20.880
Is that a peace sign?

01:11:20.880 --> 01:11:21.980
Yup.

01:11:21.980 --> 01:11:23.090
Peace, peace!

01:11:23.490 --> 01:11:27.330
Hearing that from you isn't too reassuring.

01:11:28.550 --> 01:11:31.140
Okay, so I translated "Rice as a Side Dish" into English.

01:11:31.140 --> 01:11:32.050
You what now?

01:11:32.050 --> 01:11:33.640
We're singing in English?

01:11:33.640 --> 01:11:35.440
It's the international version!

01:11:35.440 --> 01:11:36.560
Are you sure?

01:11:36.560 --> 01:11:38.540
How did you translate it?

01:11:39.640 --> 01:11:41.150
Well...

01:11:41.150 --> 01:11:45.360
I translated "<i>gohan wa sugoi yo</i>" as "rice is super."

01:11:45.720 --> 01:11:47.150
Isn't that too literal?

01:11:47.150 --> 01:11:49.160
And "<i>nan demo au yo</i>"?

01:11:49.590 --> 01:11:51.410
"<i>Bacchiri</i> just fit!"

01:11:51.730 --> 01:11:53.910
Half of that is Japanese, you know.

01:11:54.280 --> 01:11:56.450
"<i>Mushiro gohan ga okazu da yo</i>"?

01:11:56.450 --> 01:12:00.120
"<i>Mushiro</i> not so much A as B."

01:12:00.120 --> 01:12:02.470
Not the most creative sentence structure.

01:12:02.470 --> 01:12:05.370
"Not so much A as nyan."

01:12:06.430 --> 01:12:10.760
"Rice is not so much main dish as side dish."

01:12:10.760 --> 01:12:13.930
It almost sounds like rice went from a main dish to a side dish that way.

01:12:13.930 --> 01:12:16.260
What? That's not the song!

01:12:16.260 --> 01:12:17.020
Got anything better?

01:12:17.020 --> 01:12:18.530
Come on, next line!

01:12:24.600 --> 01:12:26.380
<i>I just had something.</i>

01:12:26.380 --> 01:12:28.350
<i>Something for Azu-nyan's song...</i>

01:12:28.350 --> 01:12:29.240
<i>What was it?</i>

01:12:30.200 --> 01:12:34.240
<i>I feel like it was a big step forward too...</i>

01:12:35.030 --> 01:12:39.790
What should I call you now, Yui-senpai?

01:12:48.300 --> 01:12:50.170
You sleepy, Azu-nyan?

01:12:50.170 --> 01:12:53.470
I didn't sleep very well because of this dream I had about you.

01:12:55.220 --> 01:12:57.350
Really? What kind of dream?

01:12:57.350 --> 01:12:59.620
A really weird one.

01:12:59.620 --> 01:13:00.650
I'm listening.

01:13:00.650 --> 01:13:02.160
I'm not saying.

01:13:02.160 --> 01:13:03.590
Come on!

01:13:04.150 --> 01:13:06.100
Hold on a second!

01:13:06.950 --> 01:13:08.820
What's going on, Mugi-chan?

01:13:10.150 --> 01:13:11.830
Mugi-chan!

01:13:11.830 --> 01:13:14.490
Is that your keyboard?

01:13:14.490 --> 01:13:17.050
You all brought your instruments, so...

01:13:17.050 --> 01:13:18.740
The amazing power of money.

01:13:18.740 --> 01:13:21.370
Everything's coming together now!

01:13:35.800 --> 01:13:38.350
It gets bigger every time I see it!

01:13:38.350 --> 01:13:40.940
It's still spinning every time I see it...

01:13:40.940 --> 01:13:43.230
The event's over there!

01:13:54.060 --> 01:13:55.230
Where're we playing?

01:13:55.230 --> 01:13:57.910
Look, a yakisoba stall!

01:13:57.910 --> 01:14:00.950
This time we'll need 5000 points before we can eat.

01:14:03.260 --> 01:14:05.600
Hey, Maki-chan!

01:14:07.790 --> 01:14:08.520
Ricchan!

01:14:08.520 --> 01:14:09.920
High five!

01:14:09.920 --> 01:14:12.430
What time do you guys start?

01:14:12.430 --> 01:14:13.950
Three-thirty.

01:14:13.950 --> 01:14:15.880
You play right before us.

01:14:15.880 --> 01:14:17.760
What time's Black Frill on?

01:14:18.930 --> 01:14:20.730
Wait, at four?

01:14:20.730 --> 01:14:23.420
Aren't we playing at four too?

01:14:23.420 --> 01:14:24.640
Yeah, I think so.

01:14:25.060 --> 01:14:27.430
Do we have the wrong time, Ricchan?

01:14:28.380 --> 01:14:30.920
Nah, they're both right.

01:14:31.440 --> 01:14:35.780
Black Frill's playing after us on the indoor stage,

01:14:35.780 --> 01:14:38.740
and you guys are playing on the outdoor one.

01:14:38.740 --> 01:14:40.240
Outdoor one?

01:14:40.240 --> 01:14:41.910
So not here...

01:14:41.910 --> 01:14:43.370
But here?

01:14:49.250 --> 01:14:51.460
It's got a pretty good view!

01:14:51.460 --> 01:14:52.840
This is incredible!

01:14:52.840 --> 01:14:54.780
I almost can't believe we're playing here!

01:14:54.780 --> 01:14:55.220
Yeah.

01:14:55.620 --> 01:14:58.660
I thought we might've been getting the short end of the stick out here,

01:14:58.660 --> 01:14:59.730
but this is pretty cool!

01:14:59.730 --> 01:15:00.840
Hi!

01:15:01.240 --> 01:15:03.130
Houkago Tea Time?

01:15:03.130 --> 01:15:04.490
Yes!

01:15:04.490 --> 01:15:06.770
Could you set up your instruments now, please?

01:15:07.140 --> 01:15:08.040
Japanese?

01:15:08.040 --> 01:15:10.480
He wants us to start setting up.

01:15:34.250 --> 01:15:37.130
Is it safe to plug this in?

01:15:37.630 --> 01:15:39.630
It won't shoot sparks?

01:15:39.630 --> 01:15:43.080
N-No, why would it?

01:15:43.080 --> 01:15:44.620
Help me out, Mio-senpai.

01:15:44.620 --> 01:15:48.180
Be careful. I have a bad feeling about this.

01:15:48.180 --> 01:15:50.080
Not you too!

01:15:51.520 --> 01:15:54.290
You think anyone out there knows?

01:15:54.290 --> 01:15:55.980
You want to ask the audience?!

01:15:56.990 --> 01:16:00.070
Do you want me to call the staff over?

01:16:01.030 --> 01:16:03.200
Just plug the damn thing in!

01:16:03.770 --> 01:16:04.700
Gitah!

01:16:11.760 --> 01:16:12.830
Sawako-sensei?!
Sawa-chan?!

01:16:12.830 --> 01:16:16.590
That guitar isn't even a Japanese brand!

01:16:17.500 --> 01:16:19.470
Who's that? Is she real?

01:16:19.470 --> 01:16:20.470
Why are you here?

01:16:20.860 --> 01:16:22.040
It has feet...

01:16:22.040 --> 01:16:24.180
I'm not a ghost!

01:16:24.570 --> 01:16:26.330
Why are you in London?

01:16:26.330 --> 01:16:27.920
Your honeymoon?

01:16:27.920 --> 01:16:29.920
I had some miles saved up.

01:16:30.820 --> 01:16:34.020
I've been paying for work parties with my card to earn points,

01:16:34.020 --> 01:16:36.690
but they're all expiring soon!

01:16:36.690 --> 01:16:39.510
Don't forget that I'm your club advisor too!

01:16:39.510 --> 01:16:40.790
When did you get here?

01:16:40.790 --> 01:16:41.950
Last night.

01:16:41.950 --> 01:16:42.780
And when are you going back?

01:16:43.220 --> 01:16:43.820
Tonight!

01:16:43.820 --> 01:16:45.370
Adults sure are tough.

01:16:45.370 --> 01:16:47.870
You should've told us you were here.

01:16:47.870 --> 01:16:51.330
I tried calling your hotel, but no one answered.

01:16:51.330 --> 01:16:53.880
Oh, so that was you.

01:16:53.880 --> 01:16:57.090
That aside, I brought along
special outfits for you guys!

01:16:57.540 --> 01:16:59.590
Japanese ladies ninja!

01:16:59.590 --> 01:17:00.840
Kunoichi outfits?!

01:17:00.840 --> 01:17:03.050
Wow, bravo! Bravo!

01:17:03.050 --> 01:17:04.590
No, no, please don't.

01:17:04.590 --> 01:17:06.260
Here, take a look!

01:17:06.690 --> 01:17:07.890
Nodoka-chan!

01:17:08.480 --> 01:17:09.270
And Ui too?!

01:17:10.020 --> 01:17:11.020
Even Jun!

01:17:11.540 --> 01:17:12.520
No.

01:17:14.450 --> 01:17:15.460
Okay, everyone.

01:17:15.460 --> 01:17:16.900
Standby, standby.

01:17:44.900 --> 01:17:48.050
We've had a lot of fun here in London!

01:17:48.500 --> 01:17:50.390
Very interesting!

01:17:50.390 --> 01:17:52.930
Did I say that right?

01:17:53.550 --> 01:17:56.210
We have to catch our flight soon, Yui.

01:18:03.420 --> 01:18:05.570
This will be our last song!

01:18:06.170 --> 01:18:07.870
"Rice as a Side Dish"!

01:18:08.530 --> 01:18:09.780
One, two, three, four!

01:18:26.280 --> 01:18:27.470
<i>After all that...</i>

01:18:27.470 --> 01:18:29.280
<i>...she's singing in Japanese, huh?</i>

01:19:43.500 --> 01:19:44.420
One more time!

01:19:50.840 --> 01:19:52.050
English <i>now</i>?

01:19:52.050 --> 01:19:53.350
Wow...

01:20:00.850 --> 01:20:02.720
<i>What the hell?</i>

01:20:31.510 --> 01:20:33.160
Sky high!

01:20:38.950 --> 01:20:41.200
Seriously?! "Sky high"?

01:20:41.200 --> 01:20:42.560
I got too excited!

01:20:42.560 --> 01:20:44.940
That baby was way too cute!

01:20:44.940 --> 01:20:47.360
I agree with you there, but still...

01:20:47.360 --> 01:20:49.280
That baby in the front?

01:20:49.280 --> 01:20:51.530
We're pushing our luck here!

01:20:51.530 --> 01:20:54.620
I just wanted to show off a bit!

01:20:54.620 --> 01:20:56.300
Hey, taxi!

01:21:04.980 --> 01:21:06.590
She's fast asleep.

01:21:06.590 --> 01:21:12.060
Azusa-chan worked really hard
to make sure our trip went smoothly.

01:21:13.470 --> 01:21:15.460
She must be exhausted.

01:21:32.630 --> 01:21:34.070
It's snowing!

01:21:34.650 --> 01:21:35.910
Wow, it is!

01:21:48.210 --> 01:21:50.920
I just realized something real important.

01:21:57.390 --> 01:22:00.470
We'll write the perfect song if we just be ourselves.

01:22:00.470 --> 01:22:03.060
You <i>just</i> realized that?

01:22:03.060 --> 01:22:05.690
I've been thinking that too, Yui-chan.

01:22:05.690 --> 01:22:07.020
Mugi-chan?

01:22:07.020 --> 01:22:09.920
I realized that in the beginning.

01:22:26.560 --> 01:22:29.090
Take all you want, Nodoka-chan!

01:22:29.090 --> 01:22:31.680
You could survive ten years off this.

01:22:31.680 --> 01:22:35.410
They never did get to have afternoon tea in London.

01:22:35.410 --> 01:22:36.980
That's too bad.

01:22:36.980 --> 01:22:38.550
You're telling me...

01:22:38.550 --> 01:22:40.760
But you put on a show, right?

01:22:40.760 --> 01:22:43.060
I heard! I wish I could've been there.

01:22:43.060 --> 01:22:44.350
It was so much fun!

01:22:44.730 --> 01:22:47.900
The whole class was saying the same thing.

01:22:47.900 --> 01:22:49.230
Really?

01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:52.780
Hey, I heard you put on a concert in London!

01:22:52.780 --> 01:22:53.650
How'd it go?

01:22:54.010 --> 01:22:55.070
What'd you play?

01:22:55.070 --> 01:22:56.610
"Rice as a Side Dish."

01:22:56.610 --> 01:22:58.200
What the heck?

01:22:58.200 --> 01:23:00.120
Exactly, Ichigo!

01:23:00.510 --> 01:23:05.160
I'd love to hear you guys play one last time before we graduate.

01:23:05.160 --> 01:23:07.830
Isn't the jazz workshop doing a graduation concert?

01:23:07.830 --> 01:23:08.370
Yeah.

01:23:08.370 --> 01:23:09.670
What?!

01:23:09.670 --> 01:23:10.630
Let's do it!

01:23:10.630 --> 01:23:12.340
I didn't think of that!

01:23:12.340 --> 01:23:13.670
It sounds like fun.

01:23:13.670 --> 01:23:14.540
Yeah!

01:23:14.540 --> 01:23:15.980
Where should we do it?

01:23:15.980 --> 01:23:16.990
Our club room?

01:23:16.990 --> 01:23:18.170
Come on!

01:23:18.180 --> 01:23:21.100
Can I request somewhere, then?

01:23:22.930 --> 01:23:24.520
A concert in the classroom?

01:23:25.070 --> 01:23:27.310
Yeah, on the last day of school!

01:23:27.680 --> 01:23:29.940
One last memory to send off our high school days!

01:23:29.940 --> 01:23:32.230
Wow, that takes me back!

01:23:32.230 --> 01:23:33.780
We did the same thin—

01:23:34.420 --> 01:23:35.220
Absolutely not!

01:23:35.220 --> 01:23:37.930
You'll disturb the other classes!

01:23:38.660 --> 01:23:42.490
You don't see the choir or wind ensemble performing in the classroom, do you?

01:23:42.490 --> 01:23:44.470
What's gotten into you, Sawa-chan?

01:23:44.470 --> 01:23:48.560
Ignoring that, you're asking for special treatment...

01:23:50.200 --> 01:23:52.140
that I can't grant you!

01:23:58.690 --> 01:24:00.250
No problem, Sawa-chan.

01:24:00.250 --> 01:24:02.660
As long as you understand, that's fine.

01:24:02.660 --> 01:24:04.390
Excuse us.

01:24:07.080 --> 01:24:08.220
<i>Back then...</i>

01:24:08.220 --> 01:24:11.480
<i>The details are kinda spotty,
but I know we got into some serious trouble.</i>

01:24:11.480 --> 01:24:16.230
<i>And they're nowhere near as hardcore as we were.</i>

01:24:16.230 --> 01:24:17.690
<i>They're almost sickeningly cutesy.</i>

01:24:18.320 --> 01:24:20.580
<i>They couldn't take the heat.</i>

01:24:20.580 --> 01:24:22.390
<i>They'd end up in tears.</i>

01:24:22.840 --> 01:24:24.370
<i>So I guess it's all on me...</i>

01:24:24.370 --> 01:24:25.950
<i>to protect that innocence!</i>

01:24:28.040 --> 01:24:30.210
Have your corsages done by tomorrow!

01:24:30.210 --> 01:24:32.380
Okay!

01:24:32.880 --> 01:24:34.300
Azusa!

01:24:34.300 --> 01:24:35.910
Can I borrow your scissors?

01:24:35.910 --> 01:24:37.070
Sure.

01:24:37.530 --> 01:24:38.040
Here.

01:24:38.040 --> 01:24:38.620
Thanks!

01:24:41.670 --> 01:24:43.220
You know, Azusa...

01:24:43.220 --> 01:24:44.550
Yeah?

01:24:45.190 --> 01:24:46.760
You're pretty funny sometimes.

01:24:46.760 --> 01:24:48.170
I completely forgot!

01:24:48.170 --> 01:24:50.180
I didn't do that! It was—

01:24:52.170 --> 01:24:54.730
Hey, Ui! Look what Azusa did!

01:24:54.730 --> 01:24:55.620
What it is, Jun-chan?

01:24:55.620 --> 01:24:55.750
I said I didn't do it...

01:24:55.750 --> 01:24:57.650
Look at these scissors!
I said I didn't do it...

01:24:57.650 --> 01:24:57.670
I said I didn't do it...

01:25:00.780 --> 01:25:02.570
Hi!

01:25:02.570 --> 01:25:04.370
A concert in the classroom?

01:25:04.370 --> 01:25:05.450
Yeah.

01:25:05.450 --> 01:25:08.040
But you know, since it's our classroom and all...

01:25:08.040 --> 01:25:11.080
Maybe we should do it alone...

01:25:11.080 --> 01:25:13.680
Or something...

01:25:14.380 --> 01:25:16.000
You can't do that.

01:25:16.430 --> 01:25:18.000
I want to play too!

01:25:18.000 --> 01:25:19.330
Really?

01:25:19.330 --> 01:25:20.630
Yeah!

01:25:21.030 --> 01:25:25.880
It's the last time I'll be able to play with you in front of everyone!

01:25:25.880 --> 01:25:27.520
And the last time at school too!

01:25:27.520 --> 01:25:28.760
Thank goodness!

01:25:28.760 --> 01:25:30.640
Thank you, Azu-nya—

01:25:31.300 --> 01:25:34.270
So when are we doing it, Ritsu-senpai?

01:25:39.830 --> 01:25:41.940
<i>The fated day has arrived.</i>

01:25:42.620 --> 01:25:45.530
<i>I'll protect them to my last breath!</i>

01:25:48.370 --> 01:25:50.120
We'll need another row.

01:25:51.000 --> 01:25:51.700
Should we really?

01:25:52.000 --> 01:25:52.940
Oh, right.

01:25:53.380 --> 01:25:55.000
We'll just wipe them off later.

01:26:21.850 --> 01:26:23.110
I'll never delete this!

01:26:28.760 --> 01:26:30.830
You're early today, Yamanaka-sensei.

01:26:30.830 --> 01:26:31.500
Yes.

01:26:31.500 --> 01:26:33.900
There's a lot to be done right now.

01:26:34.460 --> 01:26:36.120
Oh? What's that sound?

01:26:36.890 --> 01:26:39.540
Maybe there's construction going on.

01:26:39.540 --> 01:26:40.520
Really?

01:26:40.520 --> 01:26:42.760
That's some pretty animated construction.

01:26:44.160 --> 01:26:44.920
Yeah, right!

01:26:45.260 --> 01:26:47.150
So <i>this</i> is what you were talking about, huh?!

01:26:47.150 --> 01:26:48.110
I knew something was amiss!

01:26:48.110 --> 01:26:49.170
No, wait!
I knew something was amiss!

01:26:49.170 --> 01:26:49.180
No, wait!

01:26:50.680 --> 01:26:51.540
A concert?

01:26:51.540 --> 01:26:52.500
Yeah.

01:26:52.980 --> 01:26:54.570
I wanna see it!

01:26:58.310 --> 01:26:59.360
So...

01:26:59.360 --> 01:27:02.250
This will be our last song.

01:27:14.950 --> 01:27:17.460
Over here! It's starting!

01:27:38.810 --> 01:27:41.300
Please wait!

01:27:41.770 --> 01:27:43.270
In your dreams!

01:27:43.270 --> 01:27:46.360
It'll be over before homeroom begins!

01:28:17.220 --> 01:28:18.120
Please stop!

01:28:18.120 --> 01:28:19.020
What's going on?!

01:28:20.880 --> 01:28:22.620
Give me a copy later.

01:28:22.620 --> 01:28:23.430
Sure thing.

01:29:22.400 --> 01:29:25.500
Well, compared to your glory days,

01:29:25.500 --> 01:29:27.840
they're pretty cute.

01:30:34.500 --> 01:30:35.150
Okay!

01:30:35.640 --> 01:30:38.760
All that's left now is to finish Azu-nyan's song!

01:30:38.760 --> 01:30:41.770
"All that's left"? That's the most important thing to do.

01:30:41.770 --> 01:30:42.620
Oh, right.

01:30:42.620 --> 01:30:44.300
I wrote the melody already.

01:30:44.300 --> 01:30:45.650
Let's hear it!

01:31:13.360 --> 01:31:16.090
This is amazing, Mugi!

01:31:17.510 --> 01:31:20.250
We just need to put the lyrics together now.

01:31:20.250 --> 01:31:21.070
Yeah.

01:31:22.490 --> 01:31:26.370
We've spent so much time together that it's hard to pick out things.

01:31:26.370 --> 01:31:27.430
You said it.

01:31:27.430 --> 01:31:29.440
She's our little treasure!

01:31:29.440 --> 01:31:31.590
Let's work that in!

01:31:34.820 --> 01:31:35.740
See you!

01:31:35.740 --> 01:31:36.580
Later.
Yeah!
Bye-bye!

01:31:50.770 --> 01:31:52.180
Dinner's ready, Nee-chan.

01:31:55.550 --> 01:31:56.770
What?

01:31:56.770 --> 01:31:57.950
You got taller!

01:31:57.950 --> 01:31:59.260
Seriously?

01:32:17.330 --> 01:32:18.480
Is it done?

01:32:19.150 --> 01:32:20.510
It's done!

01:32:21.100 --> 01:32:23.720
Thank goodness! We made it in time!

01:32:23.720 --> 01:32:27.370
Hey, Yui... It's a little late to ask, but you didn't tell—

01:32:27.370 --> 01:32:28.600
She has no idea!

01:32:28.600 --> 01:32:30.560
Not even Ui knows!

01:32:31.700 --> 01:32:33.060
You know...

01:32:33.620 --> 01:32:34.820
What's up?

01:32:35.210 --> 01:32:37.160
All four of them have been...

01:32:38.160 --> 01:32:39.280
acting weird recently.

01:32:39.870 --> 01:32:41.180
Haven't they always been...

01:32:41.180 --> 01:32:42.200
a bit weird?

01:32:46.040 --> 01:32:47.370
In a different way!

01:32:48.710 --> 01:32:49.960
Like how?

01:32:51.020 --> 01:32:55.130
They drop whatever they're doing when I show up.

01:32:56.100 --> 01:32:57.960
That <i>is</i> a bit strange.

01:32:57.960 --> 01:33:01.760
And when I ask them what they're doing, they just look away.

01:33:02.160 --> 01:33:04.300
Maybe they're sending messages...

01:33:04.300 --> 01:33:05.430
to outer space!

01:33:05.820 --> 01:33:06.770
No way!

01:33:06.770 --> 01:33:11.060
Maybe they have a secret stash of sweets they're eating behind your back.

01:33:11.530 --> 01:33:12.930
That's...

01:33:14.380 --> 01:33:15.800
actually believable.

01:33:16.900 --> 01:33:19.720
I feel like they've been hiding something.

01:33:21.610 --> 01:33:22.450
Hey, Ui.

01:33:23.010 --> 01:33:24.800
Just to be sure...

01:33:24.800 --> 01:33:28.740
Yui-senpai's not repeating a year, right?

01:33:29.350 --> 01:33:30.410
No, she's not.

01:33:30.760 --> 01:33:31.660
Really?

01:33:31.660 --> 01:33:35.070
She said she was buying new tights for the ceremony.

01:33:35.070 --> 01:33:36.360
I see...

01:33:37.010 --> 01:33:40.210
Maybe she didn't actually get into college, then.

01:33:40.210 --> 01:33:41.080
What?!

01:33:41.080 --> 01:33:42.840
I know she did for sure.

01:33:43.420 --> 01:33:45.050
So what could it be?

01:33:51.750 --> 01:33:54.190
I'm sure it's nothing, Azusa-chan!

01:33:55.230 --> 01:34:04.700
<i>But hey, we met the wonderful you.</i>

01:34:09.120 --> 01:34:12.970
Something's missing from these lyrics...

01:34:17.710 --> 01:34:19.290
Onee-chan, I'm coming in!

01:34:19.810 --> 01:34:21.160
Go ahea—

01:34:21.990 --> 01:34:22.720
Um...

01:34:24.030 --> 01:34:26.310
Wait a sec!

01:34:30.090 --> 01:34:32.350
Okay, you can come in!

01:34:37.860 --> 01:34:40.990
Onee-chan, it's going to leave marks on your face again.

01:34:40.990 --> 01:34:41.940
Oh, you're right!

01:34:42.850 --> 01:34:45.000
Let's try this...

01:34:45.730 --> 01:34:47.910
Are you ready for tomorrow?

01:34:48.460 --> 01:34:49.540
Yeah!

01:34:50.780 --> 01:34:53.190
It's finally time to graduate, huh?

01:34:53.190 --> 01:34:54.370
Go to bed early tonight, okay?

01:34:54.770 --> 01:34:55.770
You too.

01:34:55.770 --> 01:34:56.590
Okay!

01:34:57.970 --> 01:34:58.630
Ui!

01:34:59.000 --> 01:35:00.120
Yeah?

01:35:01.970 --> 01:35:02.920
Thanks.

01:35:05.120 --> 01:35:08.930
I wouldn't be graduating if not for you.

01:35:12.370 --> 01:35:13.350
No problem!

01:35:14.800 --> 01:35:16.290
Good night.

01:35:16.290 --> 01:35:17.800
Night!

01:35:17.800 --> 01:35:19.760
One more thing, Ui.

01:35:20.610 --> 01:35:21.230
What is it?

01:35:21.720 --> 01:35:25.810
You think we'll all be able to drink tea together in college?

01:35:27.590 --> 01:35:30.030
Of course! I don't see why not.

01:35:30.410 --> 01:35:33.550
Really? That's good to hear.

01:35:33.550 --> 01:35:35.870
Good night for real this time.

01:35:38.820 --> 01:35:40.000
Nighty-night!

01:35:53.940 --> 01:36:03.280
<i>But hey, we met a wonderful little kitten.</i>

01:36:14.810 --> 01:36:16.790
Come on! Faster, faster!

01:36:16.790 --> 01:36:18.200
Slow down!

01:36:18.200 --> 01:36:19.160
Hurry up!

01:36:42.600 --> 01:36:43.520
Yui!

01:36:46.050 --> 01:36:47.490
The door was left open!

01:37:17.580 --> 01:37:19.280
Hey, Ricchan...

01:37:20.460 --> 01:37:22.600
You think we'll be able to play it right?

01:37:23.380 --> 01:37:28.290
I've never felt so nervous in my life!

01:37:31.260 --> 01:37:32.240
Me either...

01:37:34.530 --> 01:37:37.140
My hands are so cold!

01:37:38.470 --> 01:37:40.100
You're right...

01:37:41.720 --> 01:37:44.420
I'm nervous too!

01:37:46.030 --> 01:37:48.140
This is too much!

01:37:48.140 --> 01:37:49.340
Wanna call it off?

01:37:49.340 --> 01:37:50.880
No way!

01:37:50.880 --> 01:37:52.720
What will Azusa-chan think?

01:37:52.720 --> 01:37:55.000
She's gonna be overjoyed!

01:37:57.660 --> 01:38:00.770
I feel better knowing I'm not the only one who's worried!

01:38:01.140 --> 01:38:02.970
Of course you're not!

01:38:40.540 --> 01:38:43.940
The first time I heard you guys play,

01:38:43.940 --> 01:38:46.480
it was "Please Give Me Wings," right?

01:38:46.890 --> 01:38:49.980
That began the light music club's days of just the four of us.

01:38:50.420 --> 01:38:52.400
And then Azusa joined us!

01:38:52.400 --> 01:38:54.950
We got a lot better after that!

01:38:54.950 --> 01:38:57.740
Azusa's muting gave us a much sharper sound.

01:38:57.740 --> 01:39:00.200
Yui just throws herself at the guitar!

01:39:00.200 --> 01:39:01.730
Like you're one to speak.

01:39:02.260 --> 01:39:04.000
I see...

01:39:04.000 --> 01:39:07.120
Azu-nyan gave us wings!

01:39:09.250 --> 01:39:15.510
She's a cute, little angel who brought us happiness!

01:39:15.510 --> 01:39:16.930
An angel?

01:39:16.930 --> 01:39:18.900
You might be right!

01:39:22.580 --> 01:39:23.140
What?

01:39:24.950 --> 01:39:35.650
<i>But hey, we met a wonderful angel.</i>

01:39:35.650 --> 01:39:36.770
How's that?

01:39:36.770 --> 01:39:38.140
I love it!

01:39:38.140 --> 01:39:39.950
Isn't that a little embarrassing?

01:39:39.950 --> 01:39:41.780
No, I really like it!

01:39:41.780 --> 01:39:45.030
Maybe this song will become Azu-nyan's wings!

01:39:46.630 --> 01:39:47.500
It will!

01:39:48.100 --> 01:39:49.710
I hope.

01:39:49.710 --> 01:39:50.760
It definitely will!

01:39:50.760 --> 01:39:56.090
It's overflowing with our love for Azusa-chan!

01:39:58.200 --> 01:40:00.140
I hope she likes it.

01:40:04.680 --> 01:40:06.410
How about some tea?

01:40:06.410 --> 01:40:07.590
Sounds good.

01:40:09.260 --> 01:40:10.120
Yeah...

01:40:12.090 --> 01:40:13.980
Let's eat red-and-white bean buns!

01:40:13.980 --> 01:40:16.230
These are so good!

01:40:16.230 --> 01:40:18.830
Save this one for Azu-nyan.

01:40:20.550 --> 01:40:22.780
How should we do this?

01:40:22.780 --> 01:40:26.130
First, as the club president, I'll say:

01:40:26.130 --> 01:40:29.340
"We have a song we want you to listen to, Azusa."

01:40:29.340 --> 01:40:30.650
Okay, then what?

01:40:30.650 --> 01:40:32.050
I guess next up is Mugi.

01:40:32.050 --> 01:40:35.090
"We made it just for you, Azusa-chan."

01:40:35.090 --> 01:40:37.090
I hope I don't mess up!

01:40:37.090 --> 01:40:39.220
No laughing, Mugi-chan!

01:40:41.010 --> 01:40:42.630
Hold on a minute.

01:40:43.380 --> 01:40:45.720
Whenever we talk about this...

01:40:47.520 --> 01:40:49.160
Oh, Azusa!

01:40:49.780 --> 01:40:51.440
I'm sorry.

01:40:51.780 --> 01:40:55.410
I wanted to make the tea today.

01:40:56.650 --> 01:40:58.070
Too late now.

01:41:08.770 --> 01:41:11.080
Come over here, Azu-nyan!

01:41:55.380 --> 01:41:56.170
I get it now.

01:44:38.540 --> 01:44:41.170
Azu-nyan loved it, right?

01:44:41.170 --> 01:44:42.260
Yeah!

01:44:42.260 --> 01:44:43.060
Yeah...

01:44:43.060 --> 01:44:45.210
Are those tears I see, Akiyama-san?

01:44:45.210 --> 01:44:47.800
M-My nose is just a bit runny!

01:44:47.800 --> 01:44:50.250
This is no time to be crying, Mio-chan!

01:44:50.250 --> 01:44:51.100
She's right!

01:44:51.100 --> 01:44:53.340
We're college students now!

01:44:53.340 --> 01:44:55.820
You're both so optimistic.

01:44:55.820 --> 01:44:59.520
We need to start having more mature sweets with our tea!

01:44:59.520 --> 01:45:00.390
Exactly!

01:45:00.390 --> 01:45:01.810
That's what you meant?

01:45:03.330 --> 01:45:04.940
Look who's back with us!

01:45:04.940 --> 01:45:05.860
Oh, yeah.

01:45:05.860 --> 01:45:09.690
I heard that Death Devil song was written for an underclassman too.

01:45:09.690 --> 01:45:10.820
Really?

01:45:10.820 --> 01:45:13.300
Different strokes for different folks, huh?

01:45:13.780 --> 01:45:14.620
Wait.

01:45:14.620 --> 01:45:17.700
